{"id": "28", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "time_sec": 7.248, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1445, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0243, -0.0012, -0.0912, -0.3399, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0028, -0.0053, -0.0005, -0.2095, -0.5903, -0.0032, -0.0009, -0.4005, -0.0027, -0.0001, -0.7206, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0305, -0.0008, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.2991, -0.0309, -0.0174, -0.0528, -0.0381, -0.0059, -0.1396, -0.0179, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.1738, -0.004, -0.0, -0.2866, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0016, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.437, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.001, -0.0014, -0.0337, -0.0005, -0.0164, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0288, -0.0061, -0.0797, -0.1202, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0092, -0.0087, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0007, -0