{"id": "39", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "time_sec": 9.522, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 64