36, -0.0401, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0275, -0.0064, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.003, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.6026, -0.0068, -0.0, -0.1132, -0.6793, -0.7792, -0.053, -0.0, -0.2135, -0.0904, -0.5241, -0.0002, -0.1365, -0.0722, -0.0834, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0005, -0.0303, -0.002, -0.0034, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.5009, -0.4271, -0.34, -0.4974, -0.0, -0.0022, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0801, -0.034, -0.0016, -0.0033, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.3674, -0.0046, -0.2255, -0.0639, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.2952, -0.0059], "cumulative_logprob": -20.817, "norm_logp": -0.0857, "input_len": 732, "output_tokens": 243, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "44", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "time_sec": 9.105, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 24