{"id": "65", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "gt": "The proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold before being burned.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "time_sec": 1.23, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 13, 576, 5181, 1969, 387, 47035, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2479, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0138, -0.0012, -0.0117, -0.0276, -0.0022, -0.0237, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.208, -0.0004, -0.2794, -0.3135, -0.3522, -0.2816, -0.2781, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.0023, -0.0006, -0.2363, -0.9731, -0.0562, -0.0718, -0.0023, -0.0042, -0.0028, -0.0014, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.3146, -0.2191], "cumulative_logprob": -3.9342, "norm_logp": -0.1035, "input_len": 394, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 76.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "68", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to either:\n\n1. Remove the blue field and burn it in a peaceful manner, then bury the ashes.\n2. Fold the flag in the customary triangle fold and burn it in a proper ceremony.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n1. Remove the blue field and burn it, or\n2. Fold the flag in the customary triangle fold and burn it in a proper ceremony.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "time_sec": 1.304, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 13, 576, 5181, 1969, 387, 47035, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2479, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0138, -0.0012, -0.0117, -0.0276, -0.0022, -0.0237, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.208, -0.0004, -0.2794, -0.3135, -0.3522, -0.2816, -0.2781, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.0023, -0.0006, -0.2363, -0.9731, -0.0562, -0.0718, -0.0023, -0.0042, -0.0028, -0.0014, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.3146, -0.2191], "cumulative_logprob": -3.9342, "norm_logp": -0.1035, "input_len": 394, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "74", "question": "how to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some signs that a male coworker may be flirting with you:\n\n* He finds reasons to be near you and seek you out discreetly (Passage 3)\n* He is always staring at you and catches your eye (Passage 2)\n* He touches you unnecessarily or finds excuses to have physical contact with you (Passage 2)\n* He smiles at you excessively or without apparent reason (Passage 2)\n* He seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him (Passage 1)\n\nIf you observe these behaviors from a male coworker, it may be a sign that he is interested in you and flirting with you. However, it's essential to remember that these signs alone do not necessarily mean the person likes you romantically, and it's possible they just have a friendly interest in you. To confirm their intentions, consider observing their behavior over time, and if you feel comfortable, try initiating a conversation or asking them out.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs such as:\n1. Physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\n2. If the coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so.\n3. If the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.\n4. If the coworker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\n5. If the coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you.\n6. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admiration.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs such as:\n1. Physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\n2. If the coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so.\n3. If the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.\n4. If the coworker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\n5. If the coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you.\n6. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admiration.", "time_sec": 6.163, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3291, 421, 697, 8593, 59968, 261, 374, 87242, 448, 498, 11, 1401, 369, 11929, 1741, 438, 510, 16, 13, 27379, 3645, 429, 655, 28146, 311, 7244, 5702, 476, 646, 387, 29671, 495, 3260, 438, 21208, 2718, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 4977, 28113, 476, 13230, 429, 498, 537, 3060, 87242, 448, 1435, 11, 653, 773, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 13719, 894, 2874, 311, 5796, 498, 11, 432, 374, 264, 1841, 315, 87242, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 2677, 42532, 518, 498, 518, 975, 979, 1052, 374, 902, 1661, 2874, 369, 432, 11, 1340, 1231, 1075, 498, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 374, 14971, 518, 697, 18010, 323, 10887, 498, 700, 61404, 398, 11, 432, 594, 264, 15440, 429, 279, 1697, 13151, 498, 624, 21, 13, 42797, 894, 2874, 311, 614, 3645, 448, 498, 374, 458, 8036, 1841, 315, 36705, 476, 65839, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1499, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0282, -0.0015, -0.1228, -0.5623, -0.1146, -0.0, -0.0301, -0.0005, -0.0053, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.1868, -0.8803, -0.0186, -0.4313, -0.2841, -0.0002, -1.4534, -0.0716, -0.0017, -1.0727, -0.0739, -0.1713, -1.6956, -0.0002, -0.0048, -0.0091, -0.0012, -0.0216, -0.0694, -0.0004, -0.0014, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.001, -0.0, -0.4391, -0.0014, -0.0001, -0.9147, -0.8345, -0.3874, -0.0, -0.1143, -0.0011, -0.1057, -0.0035, -0.5654, -0.008, -0.1558, -0.0004, -0.0239, -0