{"id": "79", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief guide on how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine beer, onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper in a large pot. Bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Reduce heat to medium and cook for 10 to 12 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and place them on the preheated grill.\n7. Cook the bratwurst for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\n8. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\n\nSo, to cook brats, you first prepare the grill, then cook the bratwurst in a beer mixture before grilling them until they're done.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "time_sec": 6.672, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 624, 20, 13, 2691, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 311, 279, 3338, 624, 21, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 16, 15, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0998, -0.0, -0.0, -0.027, -0.0003, -0.2464, -0.5368, -0.4662, -0.0873, -0.0015, -0.0006, -0.0022, -0.0383, -0.1164, -0.0123, -0.0038, -0.6988, -0.0002, -0.1124, -0.0016, -0.0005, -0.0442, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.524, -0.0062, -0.0001, -0.705, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.015, -0.3002, -0.0081, -0.0116, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.9509, -0.5693, -0.2424, -0.1832, -0.0078, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0081, -0.0069, -0.3906, -0.0068, -0.0097, -0.0004, -0.0008, -0.0244, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.1423, -0.0003, -0.0015, -0.0042, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0064, -0.0001, -0.0027, -0.7659, -1.395, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.1533, -0.6044, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0163, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0078, -0.3448, -0.0339, 