{"id": "90", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that it runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Repeat step 4 to make two smears.\n6. Allow the smears to air dry.\n7. Label the slides clearly.\n8. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to sterilize the needle used to obtain the blood sample by heating it with a flame before using it. Additionally, it is essential to wear rubber gloves when handling blood to avoid coming into contact with potentially infectious materials.", "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "time_sec": 4.91, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.17, -0.0, -0.0, -0.024, -0.0011, -0.1672, -0.8695, -0.0014, -0.0027, -0.0009, -0.0235, -0.2128, -0.0881, -0.0057, -0.004, -0.366, -0.0352, -0.0003, -0.1708, -0.0109, -0.0017, -0.0035, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.272, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0075, -0.1613, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0261, -0.0048, -0.0001, -0.034, -0.0001, -0.0071, -0.013, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0224, -0.0069, -0.0009, -0.0012, -0.2653, -0.1671, -0.0018, -0.0004, -0.0144, -0.004, -0.0009, -0.0093, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.1284, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0315, -0.0146, -0.0591, -0.3655, -0.0037, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.07, -0.6468, -0.414, -0.4783, -0.0001, -0.0078, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0011, -0.1313, -0.0015, -0.0204, -0.0129, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0252, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0389, -0.7019, -0.707, -0.0486, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.015, -0.0001, -0.0017, -0.0901, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0038, -0.0009, -0.0001,