{"id": "97", "question": "typical weather in indiana", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes long, warm, humid, and wet summers, and chilly and windy winters. The temperature ranges from 22°F to 85°F throughout the year. The passages also mention snowfall and snow accumulation in specific cities, but do not provide a comprehensive overview of the typical weather in Indiana. Therefore, it is not possible to provide a complete answer based solely on the given passages.", "pred": "1. Summers are long, warm, humid, and wet.\n2. Winters are chilly and windy.\n3. It is partly cloudy year-round.\n4. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F.\n5. The temperature is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F.\n6. The wettest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of measured rain.\n7. The driest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1934 with 24.97 inches of measured rain.\n8. The most snowfall recorded in Rockford was 74.5 inches in one season.\n9. The maximum monthly precipitation was over 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes:\n\n1. Summers are long, warm, humid, and wet.\n2. Winters are chilly and windy.\n3. It is partly cloudy year-round.\n4. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F.\n5. The temperature is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F.\n6. The wettest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of measured rain.\n7. The driest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1934 with 24.97 inches of measured rain.\n8. The most snowfall recorded in Rockford was 74.5 inches in one season.\n9. The maximum monthly precipitation was over 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "time_sec": 5.87, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 14260, 9104, 304, 21591, 5646, 1447, 16, 13, 79648, 52