{"id": "116", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how water shares are transferred:\n\n1. Passage 1 states that a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. The passage also mentions that a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n2. Passage 2 outlines the steps required to transfer a Water Stock Certificate: (a) The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate, (b) the new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership, (c) a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and (d) a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner.\n3. Passage 3 provides general information about buying a home with water shares or rights, including the need to understand the steps involved in transferring water rights into the buyer's name. However, this passage does not provide specific instructions for transferring water shares.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the answer to the question is:\n\nTransferring water shares involves paying a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer, returning the Water Stock Certificate to the company, providing proof of ownership, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate in the new owner's name.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return 