{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\n\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "time_sec": 9.54, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 518, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 6839, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 23, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 11, 979, 9334, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 24, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 