{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "time_sec": 1.959, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0754, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0167, -0.0037, -0.0725, -0.2017, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.6919, -0.254, -0.0005, -0.1094, -0.009, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.8565, -0.8839, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0088, -0.0021, -0.5587, -0.0005, -0.0507, -0.0013, -0.0009, -0.01, -0.0053, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.1509, -0.0144, -0.056, -0.0026, -0.0047, -0.0002, -0.2382, -0.6988, -0.4062, -0.2226, -1.6809, -0.054, -0.2647, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0091, -0.009, -0.0097, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.3124, -0.0305, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.2287, -0.9289], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1691, "norm_logp": -0.1389, "input_len": 648, "output_tokens": 66, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "141", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "time_sec": 2.041, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0754, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0167, -0.0037, -0.0725, -0.2017, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.6919, -0.254, -0.0005, -0.1094, -0.009, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.8565, -0.8839, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0088, -0.0021, -0.5587, -0.0005, -0.0507, -0.0013, -0.0009, -0.01, -0.0053, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.1509, -0.0144, -0.056, -0.0026, -0.0047, -0.0002, -0.2382, -0.6988, -0.4062, -0.2226, -1.6809, -0.054, -0.2647, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0091, -0.009, -0.0097, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.3124, -0.0305, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.2287, -0.9289], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1691, "norm_logp": -0.1389, "input_len": 648, "output_tokens": 66, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "144", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\n\n1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "time_sec": 7.871, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 223