{"id": "159", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Switch off the device by holding down the Power button for a while.\n2. Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds until Bootloader Mode menu appears on the screen.\n3. From the menu, choose \"Factory Data Reset\" by using Volume buttons to scroll and Power key to select.\n4. Confirm the reset by pressing \"Erase Everything\".\n5. Release all keys when the process is complete.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.", "time_sec": 1.597, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 264, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 16932, 4540, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.5573, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0389, -0.0012, -0.1701, -0.1684, -0.0096, -0.0002, -0.6981, -0.0017, -0.0019, -0.0006, -0.3818, -0.1101, -0.0041, -0.0023, -0.6422, -0.0055, -0.0045, -1.0093, -0.0078, -0.0037, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.3741, -0.0229, -0.0049, -0.0017, -0.4334, -0.0019, -0.0001, -0.0045, -0.0357, -0.0277, -0.0242, -0.0001, -0.0207, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0058, -0.0004, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.001, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.5204, -0.0868], "cumulative_logprob": -5.3921, "norm_logp": -0.1037, "input_len": 638, "output_tokens": 52, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "166", "question": "what is psa levels mean", "gt": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels refer to the amount of prostate-specific antigen present in a man's blood. The level of PSA is measured in nanograms per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Normal PSA levels range between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml, and a moderate elevation in PSA levels may require further testing, such as a free PSA test, to determine the ratio of free to total PSA and help distinguish between prostate cancer and other non-cancer causes of elevated PSA. Therefore, the PSA test is used to monitor the progression of prostate cancer and to detect elevated PSA levels that may indicate prostate cancer or other prostate issues.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, and the results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, and the results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood.", "time_sec": 2.809, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 69486, 5866, 525, 264, 6629, 315, 279, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 96593, 69486, 5866, 1231, 13216, 46347, 9387, 11, 264, 2477, 66, 11705, 782, 2971, 1741, 438, 462, 9878,