{"id": "172", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften sugar, place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days. Alternatively, preheat oven to lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and remove sugar from package. Put in an ovenproof container and place in the warm oven for 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "pred": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\n\n2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "time_sec": 8.524, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 279, 5476, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 2506, 432, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 3593, 17, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 13, 576, 1429, 11050, 1616, 311, 2506, 13876, 13163, 8413, 374, 311, 2506, 432, 19046, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 11, 32894, 279, 3311, 315, 3720, 14338, 438, 1753, 438, 3204, 13, 13795, 279, 13163, 1119, 279, 24632, 5476, 3204, 773, 429, 1052, 374, 20171, 894, 3720, 3550, 1948, 279, 13163, 323, 279, 26334, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1171, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0174, -0.0009, -0.1179, -0.936, -0.0014, -