{"id": "180", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, hugging has several psychological effects. It can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Additionally, hugging can reduce worry of mortality and soothe existential fears. The use of empathy and listening skills during hugging can also create a psychological hug, making the person feel like they are receiving a real hug.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, hugging has several psychological effects. It can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Additionally, hugging can reduce worry of mortality and soothe existential fears. The use of empathy and listening skills during hugging can also create a psychological hug, making the person feel like they are receiving a real hug.", "time_sec": 2.09, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 305, 35268, 702, 3807, 23187, 6239, 13, 1084, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 11, 14269, 65164, 11, 323, 6247, 46351, 13, 22406, 11, 305, 35268, 646, 7949, 10955, 315, 28428, 323, 43176, 1782, 66639, 23209, 13, 576, 990, 315, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 2337, 305, 35268, 646, 1083, 1855, 264, 23187, 29784, 11, 3259, 279, 1697, 2666, 1075, 807, 525, 12308, 264, 1931, 29784, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0443, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0118, -0.0004, -0.0629, -0.8781, -0.0, -0.4358, -1.0366, -0.0359, -0.0133, -0.814, -1.2167, -0.6573, -1.1722, -0.0004, -1.4443, -0.0011, -0.1844, -0.0047, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0763, -0.0006, -1.4669, -1.3073, -0.0, -0.6624, -0.0002, -0.2915, -0.9376, -0.5312, -0.8602, -0.0004, -0.687, -0.5512, -0.0622, -0.3189, -0.0002, -0.4744, -1.3369, -0.8395, -0.0, -0.1021, -0.0021, -0.0025, -0.0006, -0.6123, -0.3921, -0.0007, -0.4515, -0.3687, -1.5315, -0.0135, -0.3141, -0.0722, -0.6787, -0.722, -0.0374, -0.9044, -0.0107, -0.4845, -0.0023, -0.0032, -0.1365, -0.1081, -0.775, -0.0958, -0.1567, -0.393], "cumulative_logprob": -26.792, "norm_logp": -0.3721, "input_len": 412, "output_tokens": 72, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "182", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the physiological effects of hugging are numerous and significant. Hugs affect the entire body and can potentially be compared to the effects of multiple drugs operating at once. Furthermore, the act of hugging can also have psychological effects. Empathic listening can lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships, as well as making conversation partners feel like they are receiving a hug, which can provide comfort and ease their existential fears. Overall, the psychological effects of hugging are positive and suggest that this simple gesture can have a significant impact on our emotional and physical wellbeing.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, hugging has several psychological effects. It can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Additionally, hugging can reduce worry of mortality and soothe existential fears. The use of empathy and listening skills during hugging can also create a psychological hug, making the person feel like they are receiving a real hug.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, hugging has several psychological effects. It can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Additionally, hugging can reduce worry of mortality and soothe existential fears. The use of empathy and listening skills during hugging can also create a psychological hug, making the person feel like they are receiving a real hug.", "time_sec": 2.342, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 305, 35268, 702, 3807, 23187, 6239, 13, 1084, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 11, 14269, 65164, 11, 323, 6247, 46351, 13, 22406, 11, 305, 35268, 646, 7949, 10955, 315, 28428, 323, 43176, 1782, 66639, 23209, 13, 576, 990, 315, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 2337, 305, 35268, 646, 1083, 