{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\n\n1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.", "time_sec": 8.097, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 17, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 944, 633, 697, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 311, 4057, 894, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 624, 19, 13, 9590, 697, 13078, 28147, 553, 1424, 369, 279, 61744, 1714, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 33