{"id": "233", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "pred": "- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 50 degrees in December.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, while Sausalito gets 0 inches of snow.\n- The average US city has 256 sunny days per year, while Sausalito has 256 sunny days per year.\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\n- Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, which is 30 points higher than the US average of 54.\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be described as follows:\n\n- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 50 degrees in December.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, while Sausalito gets 0 inches of snow.\n- The average US city has 256 sunny days per year, while Sausalito has 256 sunny days per year.\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\n- Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, which is 30 points higher than the US average of 54.\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.", "time_sec": 8.279, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 11017, 1447, 12, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 304, 6122, 624, 12, 576, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 304, 6652, 624, 12, 576, 1429, 15088, 59950, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 13666, 304, 6058, 448, 220, 15, 14924, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 5221, 220, 17, 21, 14924, 315, 11794, 817, 1042, 11, 1393, 328, 79074, 6357, 5221, 220, 15, 14924, 315, 11794, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 702, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 11, 1393, 328, 79074, 6357, 702, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 576, 5768, 1550, 374, 2163, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 6058, 3347, 374, 220, 19, 18, 12348, 624, 12, 328, 79074, 6357, 594, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 23, 19, 700, 315, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11, 892, 374, 220, 18, 15, 3501, 5080, 1091, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 2274, 5461, 369, 279, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 1922, 374, 3118, 389, 279, 2790, 1372, 315, 2849, 29071, 2878, 279, 6838, 2088, 315, 220, 22, 15, 12, 23, 15, 12348, 11, 323, 264, 16346, 374, 9251, 369, 2849, 315, 26541, 37093, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0272, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0178, -0.0003, -0.106, -0.576, -0.0215, -0.1857, -0.0211, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.6913, -0.0001, -0.7713, -0.0326, -0.0151, -0.1308, -0.7119, -0.9071, -0.2781, -0.117, -0.01, -0.0011, -0.2643, -0.5784, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.6341, -0.5955, -0.3142, -0.0091, -0.0011, -0.7613, -0.0026, -0.270