{"id": "236", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "pred": "- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 50 degrees in December.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, while Sausalito gets 0 inches of snow.\n- The average US city has 256 sunny days per year, while Sausalito has 256 sunny days per year.\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\n- Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, which is 30 points higher than the US average of 54.\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be described as follows:\n\n- The highes