{"id": "244", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) have several differences. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another important difference is the requirement of disability. The ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the need for it to be a substantial limit.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "time_sec": 2.615, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 