{"id": "297", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's gravitational potential energy due to its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy stored in objects due to their deformation. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane's kinetic energy in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, a baseball's kinetic energy due to its fast velocity despite its small mass, and the kinetic energy possessed by objects in motion such as cars, balls, rivers, athletes, amusement park rides, and satellites in orbit.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and rides in an amusement park.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and rides in an amusement park.", "time_sec": 2.32, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 323, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1738, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0213, -0.0008, -0.287, -0.1624, -0.0021, -0.5331, -0.2522, -0.1986, -0.9362, -0.0677, -0.0076, -0.0068, -0.4667, -0.0024, -0.6132, -0.1445, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0134, -0.0001, -0.0055, -0.0001, -0.3778, -0.9422, -0.0, -0.4163, -1.0835, -0.0039, -0.0003, -0.6908, -0.2443, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.014, -0.2529, -0.0074, -0.1584, -0.0022, -0.0009, -0.0103, -0.0019, -0.0001, -0.0079, -0.0423, -0.0, -0.342, -0.0851, -0.0256, -0.0817, -0.003, -0.0026, -0.0019, -0.0013, -0.7524, -0.0031, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.3051, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.2121, -0.6469, -0.7734, -0.0033, -0.2227, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0251, -0.1453], "cumulative_logprob": -11.7899, "norm_logp": -0.1593, "input_len": 433, "output_tokens": 74, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "299", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be installed. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater to keep it hot. This continuous loop ensures that hot water is always available.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "time_sec": 2.479, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0833, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0153, -0.0009, -0.1409, -0.892, -0.0102, -0.1536, -0.0067, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.3648, -0.5568, -0.4767, -0.0001, -0.0084, -0.0005, -0.266, -0.1171, -0.0154, -0.1867, -0.0047, -0.0531, -0.0166, -0.0, -0.2456, -0.0008, -0.0006, -0.0019, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0035, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.214, -0.7324, -0.0271, -0.2003, -0.0, -0.0538, -0.0058, -0.0109, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0807, -0.0001, -0.0162, -0.0073, -0.03, -0.0001, -0.3892, -0.1455, -0.1736, -0.0048, -0.0628, -0.0005, -0.0528, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.002, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0747, -0.2833], "cumulative_logprob": -6.1985, "norm_logp": -0.0816, "input_len": 446, "output_tokens": 76, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 75.95, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "301", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how you can make a hot water heater circulate:\n\n1. Install a recirculating pump: As described in passage 3, a recirculating pump can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\n2. Use a demand-based system: According to passage 3, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor. This means that the pump will only run when there is a demand for hot water, rather than constantly running.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to make a hot water heater circulate, but rather describe the concept of circulation and the different types of systems used to achieve it.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "time_sec": 2.707, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0833, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0153, -0.0009, -0.1409, -0.892, -0.0102, -0.1536, -0.0067, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.3648, -0.5568, -0.4767, -0.0001, -0.0084, -0.0005, -0.266, -0.1171, -0.0154, -0.1867, -0.0047, -0.0531, -0.0166, -0.0, -0.2456, -0.0008, -0.0006, -0.0019, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0035, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.214, -0.7324, -0.0271, -0.2003, -0.0, -0.0538, -0.0058, -0.0109, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0807, -0.0001, -0.0162, -0.0073, -0.03, -0.0001, -0.3892, -0.1455, -0.1736, -0.0048, -0.0628, -0.0005, -0.0528, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.002, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0747, -0.2833], "cumulative_logprob": -6.1985, "norm_logp": -0.0816, "input_len": 446, "output_tokens": 76, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "303", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "time_sec": 2.599, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645],