{"id": "310", "question": "avg cost to install a second floor in a house", "gt": "Hiring a remodeling contractor to build a second floor addition can cost between $100-$300 a square foot for a typical addition, but the cost can go as high as $400-$500 per square foot depending on the complexity, quality of materials and local labor rates. Building a second floor can cost at least 20 percent more than building the same square footage at ground level.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the average cost to install a second floor in a house can range from $100 to $400 per square foot, depending on complexity, quality of materials, and local labor rates.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the average cost to install a second floor in a house can range from $100 to $400 per square foot, depending on complexity, quality of materials, and local labor rates.", "time_sec": 1.779, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 5461, 2783, 311, 4582, 264, 2086, 6422, 304, 264, 3753, 646, 2088, 504, 400, 16, 15, 15, 311, 400, 19, 15, 15, 817, 9334, 4478, 11, 11649, 389, 23094, 11, 4271, 315, 7236, 11, 323, 2205, 9327, 7813, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1543, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0121, -0.0022, -0.022, -0.0322, -0.1608, -0.0005, -0.0037, -0.0158, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0094, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.4181, -0.2872, -0.1077, -0.0201, -0.1452, -0.003, -0.0003, -0.4778, -0.0037, -0.4578, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5931, -0.0782, -0.0002, -0.6169, -0.0054, -0.0116, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0069, -0.021, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.014, -0.6396], "cumulative_logprob": -4.3286, "norm_logp": -0.0921, "input_len": 669, "output_tokens": 47, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "318", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "pred": "3. Using Tax Software: If you e-filed your return, wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you provide your email address, most tax software will send you an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return. Software programs also typically have an application that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can check taxes were filed in the following ways:\n\n1. Online: You can check the status of your tax return online by using the IRS2Go application for Apple users or by visiting the IRS website. If you e-filed your taxes, you should be able to get a refund status within 72 hours. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\n2. Over the Phone: You can also check the status of your tax return by phoning the IRS. It takes time for the IRS to process your taxes, so give them adequate time before checking on the status of your refund.\n\n3. Using Tax Software: If you e-filed your return, wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you provide your email address, most tax software will send you an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return. Software programs also typically have an application that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account.", "time_sec": 8.36, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 1779, 13125, 1033, 12729, 304, 279, 2701, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 8105, 25, 1446, 646, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 3742, 470, 2860, 553, 1667, 279, 33383, 17, 10850, 3766, 369, 8162, 3847, 476, 553, 16721, 279, 33383, 3910, 13, 1416, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 1265, 387, 2952, 311, 633, 264, 20965, 2639, 2878, 220, 22, 17, 4115, 13, 1416, 498, 75210, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 686, 614, 311, 3783, 220, 18, 476, 220, 19, 5555, 1283, 32759, 304, 697, 13125, 382, 17, 13, 6065, 279, 14307, 25, 1446, 646, 1083, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 3742, 470, 553, 1319, 19744, 279, 33383, 13, 1084, 4990, 882, 369, 279, 33383, 311, 1882, 697, 13125, 11, 773, 2968, 1105, 25532, 882, 1573, 13295, 389, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 20965, 382, 18, 13, 12091, 15190, 4377, 25, 1416, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 470, 11, 3783, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 1283, 279, 33383, 25498, 22567, 315, 697, 470, 13, 1416, 498, 3410, 697, 2551, 2621, 11, 1429, 3742, 3162, 686, 3624, 498, 458, 2551, 19539, 979, 279, 33383, 26344, 697, 3742, 470, 13, 4377, 7468, 1083, 11136, 614, 458, 3766, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 470, 553, 8392, 1119, 697, 2692, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0995, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0445, -0.0009, -0.0802, -0.3038, -0.0032, -0.0124, -1.0854, -0.1875, -0.0002, -1.0504, -0.3691, -0.0002, -0.0331, -0.1408, -0.0034, -0.0003, -1.0038, -0.3926, -0.6157, -0.0027, -0.5679, -0.028, -0.004, -0.0017, -0.3283, -0.652, -0.0462, -0.5694, -1.1772, -0.7635, -0.8937, -0.0428, -0.1169