{"id": "321", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of an individual's lifestyle and daily activities, specifically the amount of greenhouse gases produced, such as carbon dioxide, as a result of those activities. The carbon footprint is typically measured in tons of CO2 released into the atmosphere. The passages also mention that reducing one's carbon footprint can have a significant impact on the environment, even with seemingly small changes. Additionally, the average carbon footprint is mentioned to be around 6 tons per year, with a higher amount in the US due to automobile emissions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of human activities. It quantifies the total amount of greenhouse gases produced by various human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. This measurement helps in understanding the environmental effect of lifestyle choices, such as using energy for heating, consuming food, and driving vehicles. Reducing carbon footprint involves making changes in daily activities to decrease the amount of greenhouse gases produced, which can lead to a significant positive impact on the environment.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of human activities. It quantifies the total amount of greenhouse gases produced by various human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. This measurement helps in understanding the environmental effect of lifestyle choices, such as using energy for heating, consuming food, and driving vehicles. Reducing carbon footprint involves making changes in daily activities to decrease the amount of greenhouse gases produced, which can lead to a significant positive impact on the environment.", "time_sec": 4.462, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2456, 315, 12499, 42872, 374, 311, 6629, 279, 12158, 5421, 315, 3738, 7488, 13, 1084, 10272, 9606, 279, 2790, 3311, 315, 36547, 44512, 8947, 553, 5257, 3738, 7488, 2878, 264, 2661, 882, 4034, 11, 11136, 16878, 304, 19608, 315, 12499, 39489, 320, 8281, 17, 8, 5880, 1119, 279, 16566, 13, 1096, 18662, 8609, 304, 8660, 279, 12158, 2456, 315, 18899, 11454, 11, 1741, 438, 1667, 4802, 369, 23579, 11, 34108, 3607, 11, 323, 9842, 11474, 13, 3731, 58044, 12499, 42872, 17601, 3259, 4344, 304, 7298, 7488, 311, 18472, 279, 3311, 315, 36547, 44512, 8947, 11, 892, 646, 2990, 311, 264, 5089, 6785, 5421, 389, 279, 4573, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3989, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0172, -0.002, -0.0402, -0.3364, -0.3064, -0.0001, -0.6011, -0.0005, -0.4391, -0.7141, -0.0231, -0.0025, -0.1113, -0.0005, -0.0038, -1.2603, -0.0022, -0.5089, -0.6042, -0.8492, -0.0035, -0.0046, -0.7302, -0.0289, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.4609, -0.4343, -0.1247, -0.1865, -0.018, -0.1409, -0.0, -0.0306, -0.0139, -0.0018, -0.1531, -0.3359, -0.1477, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.0552, -0.0, -0.034, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.1547, -0.0052, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0104, -1.1046, -0.3962, -0.3111, -0.4789, -0.1229, -0.1769, -0.4079, -0.764, -0.0014, -1.0193, -0.1976, -0.6725, -0.5226, -0.0, -1.1367, -0.6327, -0.9549, -0.04, -0.774, -0.8359, -0.1076, -0.2238, -0.0844, -0.2614, -0.3954, -0.1863, -1.2794, -0.0001, -1.1299, -0.0167, -0.7176, -0.7066, -0.3802, -0.4895, -0.6996, -0.125, -0.1862, -0.6729, -0.1128, -0.513, -0.0, -0.3026, -0.0037, -0.236, -0.3187, -0.5858, -0.034, -1.0794, -0.0, -0.6295, -0.6835, -0.6503, -0.183, -0.002, -0.0108, -0.0002, -0.0824, -0.228], "cumulative_logprob": -33.1706, "norm_logp": -0.2884, "input_len": 515, "output_tokens": 115, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "325", "question": "how well do patterned rollers work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that patterned rollers can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, as they can produce a random pattern of texture that is often desired in faux finishing techniques. The third passage provides instructions for creating a DIY texture roller by modifying an existing roller pad with rubber bands to create clumps and random patterns, which can be used to apply paint and create a textured finish.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How well do patterned rollers work?\" is:\n\nThey can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, especially when used with faux finishing techniques.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, patterned rollers can work well, but the effectiveness may vary depending on the type of roller and the user's skin type. For example, the Dermaroller worked well for the user on their face, but caused redness on their neck and chest. The Basic Texture Roller, on the other hand, can be effective for applying texture to walls, but requires careful adjustment of the rubber bands to maintain the desired pattern.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, patterned rollers can work well, but the effectiveness may vary depending on the type of roller and the user's skin type. For example, the Dermaroller worked well for the user on their face, but caused redness on their neck and chest. The Basic Texture Roller, on the other hand, can be effective for applying texture to walls, but requires careful adjustment of the rubber bands to maintain the desired pattern.", "time_sec": 3.021, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 5383, 291, 88613, 646, 975, 1632, 11, 714, 279, 26279, 1231, 13289, 11649, 389, 279, 943, 315, 28451, 323, 279, 1196, 594, 6787, 943, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 75408, 277, 69396, 6439, 1632, 369, 279, 1196, 389, 862, 3579, 11, 714, 8881, 2518, 2090, 389, 862, 12975, 323, 15138, 13, 576, 14625, 18757, 44542, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 646, 387, 7373, 369, 18950, 10434, 311, 14285, 11, 714, 7460, 16585, 27075, 315, 279, 22674, 20892, 311, 10306, 279, 12685, 5383, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0424, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0207, -0.002, -0.0337, -0.4868, -0.0, -0.0404, -1.0396, -0.1918, -0.4596, -0.8637, -0.9955, -1.1549, -0.1398, -0.9802, -0.1452, -0.5715, -0.0, -0.1108, -0.9794, -0.2587, -0.7691, -0.1651, -0.138, -1.6166, -0.0675, -0.4738, -0.7533, -0.1406, -0.8716, -0.2989, -0.0018, -0.5921, -0.1029, -0.0001, -0.0009, -1.8423, -0.6618, -0.197, -0.5143, -0.5635, -0.6486, -0.1791, -0.0025, -0.6508, -0.104, -0.8433, -0.1222, -0.0002, -0.1662, -0.1092, -0.001, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.7787, -1.0659, -0.4395, -0.0011, -0.0003, -0.8101, -0.4358, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7105, -0.9407, -1.4267, -1.0094, -0.6327, -1.2399, -0.4677, -0.0108, -0.4651, -0.4894, -0.8257, -1.3512, -0.5768, -0.1225, -0.43, -0.0199, -0.0016, -0.7163, -0.1402, -0.2221, -0.5344, -0.1257, -0.022, -0.5667], "cumulative_logprob": -37.6953, "norm_logp": -0.4142, "input_len": 530, "output_tokens": 91, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "331", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\n\nThe ice water bath helps to stop the cooking process and cool down the potatoes quickly, making the skin easier to peel off.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.", "time_sec": 4.102, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11