{"id": "334", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Additionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to remove it.\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\n5. If you yank the tick away too quickly, you might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n\nAdditionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.", "time_sec": 6.155, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4248, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 1181, 6414, 11, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 624, 18, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 311, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 498, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 2238, 6157, 11, 498, 2578, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240