0.0007, -0.9851, -0.0038, -0.0144, -0.0179, -0.0067, -0.0036, -0.0834, -0.0002, -0.1568, -1.34, -0.2527, -0.1919, -0.0032, -0.0785, -0.4889, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.3489, -0.459, -0.3444, -0.0015, -0.001, -0.1957, -0.0796, -0.5232, -0.0003, -0.0015, -0.0311, -0.0208, -0.0007, -0.0404, -0.0372, -0.0319, -0.0371, -0.7292, -0.9573, -0.1616, -0.1375, -0.6365, -0.0015, -0.0009, -0.0003, -0.8443, -0.115], "cumulative_logprob": -26.9201, "norm_logp": -0.1584, "input_len": 627, "output_tokens": 170, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "339", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\n1. **Grilled Ribs:**\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\n2. **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs:**\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\n\n3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "time_sec": 11.187, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 22471, 10823, 45277, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 34860, 287, 279, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 369, 8628, 4225, 7455, 389, 678, 11067, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 14263, 279, 55149, 25, 19219, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 1447