{"id": "351", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "time_sec": 2.764, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 20699, 5707, 1661, 2473, 476, 3871, 11, 6388, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 3409, 8668, 91039, 18564, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 3643, 432, 8661, 311, 4559, 279, 2562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2516, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0213, -0.0008, -0.0522, -0.0704, -0.0005, -0.4984, -0.0, -0.0105, -1.018, -0.1892, -0.1256, -0.3879, -0.6857, -0.003, -0.6886, -1.6127, -0.0552, -0.6882, -0.8524, -0.3549, -0.0002, -0.2071, -0.731, -0.4877, -0.4101, -1.5581, -0.1768, -0.1011, -0.0381, -0.7271, -0.0117, -0.1604, -0.0191, -0.0372, -0.2484, -0.5842, -0.2579, -0.2818, -0.7941, -0.0213, -0.2125, -1.066, -0.0161, -0.0, -0.2606, -0.3815, -0.8008, -0.0008, -0.0572, -0.2157, -0.8515, -0.0037, -1.0639, -0.687, -0.4462, -0.0142, -0.0107, -0.0, -0.4142, -0.2214, -0.2435, -0.021, -0.0007, -0.05, -0.0371, -0.009, -0.0002, -1.1727, -0.4442, -0.2597, -0.1428, -0.2458, -0.0353, -0.0263, -0.1064, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0505, -1.1396], "cumulative_logprob": -25.1293, "norm_logp": -0.3065, "input_len": 442, "output_tokens": 82, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "354", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "time_sec": 2.69, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 20699, 5707, 1661, 2473, 476, 3871, 11, 6388, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 3409, 8668, 91039, 18564, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 3643, 432, 8661, 311, 4559, 279, 2562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2516, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0213, -0.0008, -0.0522, -0.0704, -0.0005, -0.4984, -0.0, -0.0105, -1.018, -0.1892, -0.1256, -0.3879, -0.6857, -0.003, -0.6886, -1.6127, -0.0552, -0.6882, -0.8524, -0.3549, -0.0002, -0.2071, -0.731, -0.4877, -0.4101, -1.5581, -0.1768, -0.1011, -0.0381, -0.7271, -0.0117, -0.1604, -0.0191, -0.0372, -0.2484, -0.5842, -0.2579, -0.2818, -0.7941, -0.0213, -0.2125, -1.066, -0.0161, -0.0, -0.2606, -0.3815, -0.8008, -0.0008, -0.0572, -0.2157, -0.8515, -0.0037, -1.0639, -0.687, -0.4462, -0.0142, -0.0107, -0.0, -0.4142, -0.2214, -0.2435, -0.021, -0.0007, -0.05, -0.0371, -0.009, -0.0002, -1.1727, -0.4442, -0.2597, -0.1428, -0.2458, -0.0353, -0.0263, -0.1064, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0505, -1.1396], "cumulative_logprob": -25.1293, "norm_logp": -0.3065, "input_len": 442, "output_tokens": 82, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "357", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "An ad hominem fallacy occurs when someone attacks the character, motive, or other personal attribute of the person making an argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. This is often done to invalidate their arguments by associating their character with the soundness of their argument. On the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy, which is a type of ad hominem attack, occurs when a person's integrity or intelligence is attacked before the merits of a case can be considered, effectively redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The key difference is that the ad hominem fallacy occurs during the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy happens before the argument begins.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The key difference is that the ad hominem fallacy occurs during the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy happens before the argument begins.", "time_sec": 3.678, "record_process": true, "toke