{"id": "375", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used in a variety of ways both industrially and medically. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for numerous chemicals. Medically, DMSO is applied to the skin as an anti-inflammatory and general pain reliever, most commonly for muscles and joints. It is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and skin ulcers. DMSO has the unique ability to penetrate skin and tissue, allowing it to enter the bloodstream.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "time_sec": 4.146, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 320, 12927, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 8, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 25266, 