{"id": "385", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 2:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. Select the data that you wish to sort by (in this case, the Product column (column B)) and choose alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all the cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n\nTherefore, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use either method described above.", "pred": "1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "time_sec": 7.116, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 279, 21029, 10834, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 20, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3241, 11, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 4292, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 979, 498, 470, 311, 279, 45886, 11, 279, 821, 1265, 387, 10615, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1832, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0574, -0.0012, -0.124, -0.3698, -0.0117, -0.0031, -0.0298, -0.0012, -0.027, -0.0, -0.347, -0.4588, -0.0067, -0.0027, -0.3343, -0.0061, -0.0002, -0.8876, -0.609, -0.1136, -0.7003, -0.2071, -0.5764, -0.8778, -0.0403, -0.3549, -0.0035, -0.181,