{"id": "421", "question": "how to find pictures you deleted on your messaging on iphone", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain information on how to find pictures that have been deleted from the Messages app on an iPhone. The first passage discusses deleting text message conversations, while the second and third passages focus on recovering deleted photos from an iPhone or iCloud backup. None of the passages provide instructions on how to retrieve deleted pictures from the Messages app.", "pred": "1. Open the Messages app on your iPhone.\n2. Swipe across the conversation to find the deleted photo.\n3. Tap the Delete button to permanently delete the entire conversation.\n4. If you want to recover the deleted photo, you can use a data recovery tool like iPhone Data Recovery.\n5. Run the data recovery tool and choose the \"Recover from iCloud Backup File\" mode.\n6. Sign in to your iCloud account with your account and password.\n7. Choose the deleted photo and click the \"Recover\" button to get it back to your computer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to find pictures you deleted on your messaging on iPhone, you can use the following steps:\n\n1. Open the Messages app on your iPhone.\n2. Swipe across the conversation to find the deleted photo.\n3. Tap the Delete button to permanently delete the entire conversation.\n4. If you want to recover the deleted photo, you can use a data recovery tool like iPhone Data Recovery.\n5. Run the data recovery tool and choose the \"Recover from iCloud Backup File\" mode.\n6. Sign in to your iCloud account with your account and password.\n7. Choose the deleted photo and click the \"Recover\" button to get it back to your computer.", "time_sec": 5.266, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1477, 9185, 498, 11062, 389, 697, 29522, 389,