{"id": "423", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "time_sec": 2.332, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 95129, 320, 58278, 5643, 6119, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 5257, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 11, 438, 817, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1771, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.015, -0.002, -0.0552, -0.2882, -0.5407, -0.1889, -0.0126, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0809, -0.0057, -0.0496, -0.0328, -0.0, -0.8112, -0.0055, -0.6341, -0.8746, -0.005, -0.2973, -0.0067, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0855, -0.0032, -0.01, -0.1186, -0.0179, -0.0, -0.0042, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0147, -0.0, -0.4518, -0.0092, -0.0099, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0008, -0.0112, -0.0, -0.0344, -0.3576, -0.1238, -0.4