{"id": "433", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\n\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth to shine silver jewelry that is merely dull or starting to discolor. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. Pat the jewelry dry with a soft cloth.\n3. Soak tarnished silver jewelry in a saltwater solution of two cups of hot water. This method is gentle and can remove tarnish without abrading the silver. Make sure the gemstones will not be affected by the solution before submerging them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to clean other types of jewelry, such as gold or platinum, or what to do if the tarnish is heavy or if the jewelry has intricate designs that may be damaged during cleaning.", "pred": "4. For silver jewelry, you can pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. If your silver is lightly tarnished, the salt bath should take the tarnish right off. If you're cleaning a lot of jewelry at once, you can use more water. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use a few different methods:\n\n1. For items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n\n2. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (not paper towels, which can scratch).\n\n3. For diamonds, the best way to clean them is with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth.\n\n4. For silver jewelry, you can pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. If your silver is lightly tarnished, the salt bath should take the tarnish right off. If you're cleaning a lot of jewelry at once, you can use more water. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "time_sec": 9.418, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 2421, 2155, 5413, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 3589, 429, 525, 16234, 40530, 11, 89394, 11, 476, 5916, 311, 2560, 789, 11, 6514, 264, 2421, 21025, 315, 23034, 12000, 26785, 448, 8205, 3015, 323, 23604, 279, 30717, 304, 264, 8413, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 30717, 11, 1221, 73241, 304, 7010, 3015, 323, 11522, 448, 264, 27292, 3080, 9058, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 43822, 86480, 812, 11, 6514, 264, 24937, 315, 2326, 5479, 27815, 38862, 311, 825, 949, 3015, 13, 44856, 279, 14961, 323, 3796, 279, 31881, 448, 264, 8413, 11, 57920, 12577, 27292, 320, 1921, 5567, 52884, 11, 892, 646, 18778, 3593, 18, 13, 1752, 48051, 11, 279, 1850, 1616, 311, 4240, 1105, 374, 448, 8205, 773, 9667, 3015, 323, 264, 8413, 30117, 28300, 15625, 476, 2310, 25507, 36061, 13, 7135, 432, 9058, 448, 264, 8413, 27292, 382, 19, 13, 1752, 14961, 30717, 11, 498, 646, 4914, 1378, 25374, 315, 4017, 3015, 1119, 264, 19212, 13, 1096, 1714, 4278, 438, 264, 21700, 34194, 261, 429, 28160, 86480, 812, 2041, 668, 81, 2228, 279, 14961, 13, 1416, 697, 14961, 374, 33404, 86480, 3304, 11, 279, 12021, 8885, 1265, 1896, 279, 86480, 812, 1