{"id": "450", "question": "how is a caldera different from a crater", "gt": "A caldera is a large depression caused by volcanic activity when a chamber of magma and lava gets emptied. This cavity creates pressure and the overground rocks collapse to create a large depression. On the other hand, a volcanic crater is a bowl-like structure at the top of a volcano around the opening that is used for the eruption of magma and lava. This is a depression that is the result of sinking in of the rocks because of high pressure and it typically has the opening through which lava and ash flows upwards. Craters can also be caused by impacts from meteorites, and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a caldera is different from a crater in how they are formed. Craters are caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred kilometers across. In contrast, calderas are formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, resulting in a large, circular depression.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a caldera is different from a crater in how they are formed. Craters are caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred kilometers across. In contrast, calderas are formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, resulting in a large, circular depression.", "time_sec": 2.312, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 1620, 97903, 374, 2155, 504, 264, 74707, 304, 1246, 807, 525, 14122, 13, 4553, 11535, 525, 8881, 553, 24905, 504, 41042, 3611, 323, 646, 2088, 304, 1379, 504, 1602, 2613, 311, 3807, 7739, 40568, 3941, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 1620, 1107, 300, 525, 14122, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 264, 65206, 979, 279, 63505, 24220, 86358, 11, 12942, 304, 264, 3460, 11, 26931, 18210, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1247, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0219, -0.0009, -0.057, -0.0623, -0.0046, -0.0, -0.4381, -0.3337, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.202, -0.6938, -0.005, -0.003, -0.0, -0.0563, -0.7258, -0.0006, -0.0348, -0.1959, -0.0, -0.0117, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.5782, -0.0091, -0.066, -0.0265, -0.0002, -0.0089, -0.0124, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0045, -0.0005, -0.4309, -0.0095, -0.254, -0.8481, -0.0014, -0.0001, -0.5318, -0.0018, -0.0002, -0.0098, -0.5757, -0.6556, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0101, -0.0006, -0.0218, -0.0276, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0022, -0.5548, -0.4616, -0.0001, -0.0312, -0.0327, -1.0398, -0.0216, -0.0018, -1.0462, -1.337], "cumulative_logprob": -11.5885, "norm_logp": -0.161, "input_len": 623, "output_tokens": 72, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "452", "question": "how is a caldera different from a crater", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a caldera is a large depression made due to volcanic activity, while a volcanic crater is a bowl-like structure at the top of a volcano that allows for the eruption of magma and lava. The primary difference between the two is the method of formation. Calderas are formed when a magma chamber collapses, resulting in a large depression, while craters are formed by impacts from meteorites.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a caldera is different from a crater in how they are formed. Craters are caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred kilometers across. In contrast, calderas are formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, resulting in a large, circular depression.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a caldera is different from a crater in how they are formed. Craters are caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred kilometers across. In contrast, calderas are formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, resulting in a large, circular depression.", "time_sec": 2.342, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 1620, 97903, 374, 2155, 504, 264, 74707, 304, 1246, 807, 525, 14122, 13, 4553, 11535, 525, 8881, 553, 24905, 504, 41042, 3611, 323, 646, 2088, 304, 1379, 504, 1602, 2613, 311, 3807, 7739, 40568, 3941, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 1620, 1107, 300, 525, 14122, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 264, 65206, 979, 279, 63505, 24220, 86358, 11, 12942, 304, 264, 3460, 11, 26931, 18210, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1247, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0219, -0.0009, -0.057, -0.0623, -0.0046, -0.0, -0.4381, -0.3337, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.202, -0.6938, -0.005, -0.003, -0.0, -0.0563, -0.7258, -0.0006, -0.0348, -0.1959, -