{"id": "490", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can track who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as their favorite.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "time_sec": 4.624, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 429, 13918, 4694, 1608, 23150, 13, 3776, 1741, 3910, 9733, 374, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 13, 2014, 990, 419, 3910, 11, 