{"id": "495", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "gt": "Salary exchange pension contributions, also known as salary sacrifice, is a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This can allow both employers and employees to save money. The salary that is waived under the salary exchange is equal to the value of the regular pension contribution made. For example, it could be 7.5% or 9% of the pay, depending on the pension scheme. The employer then pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money. Employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. The value of the salary waived under the Salary Exchange is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution to USS, USPAS, or SGSS, excluding additional contributions. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 October 2011 is 7.5% of their pay, and for members of USPAS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 August 2011 is 9%.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money. Employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. The value of the salary waived under the Salary Exchange is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution to USS, USPAS, or SGSS, excluding additional contributions. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 October 2011 is 7.5% of their pay, and for members of USPAS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 August 2011 is 9%.", "time_sec": 5.873, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 16107, 9289, 27681, 19026, 21058, 458, 9364, 38327, 311, 2968, 705, 949, 315, 862, 16107, 476, 12037, 304, 9289, 369, 264, 27681, 8160, 7171, 553, 862, 19136, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 3581, 3220, 13, 20782, 388, 2291, 4722, 5055, 21674, 96004, 320, 44947, 82, 8, 438, 264, 1102, 315, 12515, 862, 8256, 264, 11046, 16107, 13, 576, 897, 315, 279, 16107, 81482, 1212, 279, 41758, 18705, 374, 6144, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 9364, 594, 5792, 27681, 18527, 311, 38508, 11, 2274, 47, 1911, 11, 476, 29626, 1220, 11, 43778, 5107, 19026, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 369, 3613, 315, 38508, 11, 279, 5792, 18527, 448, 2456, 504, 220, 16, 6527, 220, 17, 15, 16, 16, 374, 220, 22, 13, 20, 4, 315, 862, 2291, 11, 323, 369, 3613, 315, 2274, 47, 1911, 11, 279, 5792, 18527, 448, 2456, 504, 220, 16, 6156, 220, 17, 15, 16, 16, 374, 220, 24, 14360, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.5777, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0193, -0.0007, -0.0956, -0.1157, -0.0005, -0.5547, -0.0001, -0.5776, -0.3807, -0.5631, -0.4887, -0.0001, -0.0502, -0.0014, -0.0622, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0053, -0.1315, -0.0148, -0.0367, -0.0625, -0.0, -0.0055, -0.0028, -0.0235, -0.252, -0.0003, -0.0393, -0.0001, -0.0145, -0.8458, -0.3735, -0.4822, -0.2147, -0.2153, -0.0007, -0.0637, -0.0001, -0.2426, -0.01, -0.3231, -0.8287, -0.0001, -0.6685, -0.0137, -0.4044, -0.0012, -0.0443, -0.034, -0.0037, -0.0009, -0.005, -0.2201, -0.002, -0.0009, -0.0333, -0.0492, -0.0582, -0.0003, -0.008, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0606, -0.6831, -1.5749, -0.0142, -0.0139, -0.1843, -0.0609, -0.5346, -0.2934, -0.5315, -0.0001, -0.078, -0.1634, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.7525, -0.0, -0.0266, -0.4884, -0.0206, -0.0002, 