{"id": "503", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main factors that contribute to oily skin are:\n\n1. Genetics: According to passage 1, oily skin is hereditary, meaning that if one's parents have oily skin, they are more likely to experience it themselves.\n2. Hormonal shifts: Passage 1 suggests that hormonal changes in the body can cause oily skin to come and go.\n3. Diet: While diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin, according to passage 1.\n4. Poor hygiene: Passage 2 mentions that poor hygiene and topical applications can contribute to oily skin.\n5. Combination skin: Passage 3 defines different skin types, including combination skin, which can be prone to oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone.\n\nThere is no additional information provided in the passages to suggest other factors that might contribute to oily skin. Therefore, the answer to the question is based on the information provided in the passages.", "pred": "1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\n\n1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.", "time_sec": 5.849, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 74126, 41822, 25, 1416, 697, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 5080, 6012, 429, 498, 686, 1083, 614, 77471, 6787, 624, 17, 13, 91108, 24202, 28635, 25, 1416, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 387, 803, 5435, 311, 73118, 4344, 304, 697, 2487, 4751, 1091, 55004, 624, 18, 13, 85856, 6787, 25, 4329, 1251, 614, 264, 10601, 315, 6787, 4494, 11, 892, 646, 2924, 77471, 5671, 1075, 279, 350, 77763, 320, 77, 960, 11, 51254, 11, 323, 45075, 568, 1096, 943, 315, 6787, 646, 8193, 38432, 18840, 657, 70928, 11, 3691, 35810, 11, 323, 41199, 6787, 624, 19, 13, 44673, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 25, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 10542, 421, 279, 5590, 1880, 374, 4152, 311, 5810, 43147, 476, 7852, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 624, 20, 13, 26212, 25, 10328, 9968, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 11, 432, 1558, 537, 5961, 5240, 77471, 6787, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0432, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0152, -0.0009, -0.0593, -0.6342, -0.1191, -0.0097, -0.0734, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3326, -0.5692, -0.0126, -0.0004, -1.0809, -0.9486, -0.2072, -0.9374, -0.3418, -0.2586, -0.0399, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7347, -0.2026, -0.0043, -0.6801, -0.7032, -0.3941, -0.0006, -0.1273, -0.563, -0.0185, -0.1471, -0.0, -1.2351, -0.0119, -0.0, -0.0081, -0.00