{"id": "507", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. The floor is home to various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines.\n2. It supports a diverse range of flora, including bananas which grow on vines.\n3. The floor is characterized by high humidity due to the heavy rainfall typical of tropical rainforests.\n4. The rapid decomposition of organic matter on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. The floor is home to various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines.\n2. It supports a diverse range of flora, including bananas which grow on vines.\n3. The floor is characterized by high humidity due to the heavy rainfall typical of tropical rainforests.\n4. The rapid decomposition of organic matter on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "time_sec": 3.353, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 340