{"id": "521", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA raffle is a game of chance where participants buy tickets with a unique number, and a prize is awarded to the holder of the winning ticket drawn at random. In a reverse raffle, the process is similar, but the tickets are numbered from 1 to approximately 55, and tables consist of 20 individuals, constituting one complete ticket at $1000, with two $500 prizes available. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, with 50% going to the winner of the random draw and the remaining 50% going to a charitable cause.\n\nTherefore, raffles typically involve buying tickets with unique numbers, and a random draw determines the winner, with a percentage of the proceeds often going to a charitable cause.", "pred": "3. **Cash Tip Board Raffles**: These are included with the ticket price and offer the chance to win $10,000.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, raffles work as follows:\n\n1. **Reverse Raffle**: In a reverse raffle, participants buy tickets with numbers from 1 to approximately 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket worth $1000. There are two $500 prizes: one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\n\n2. **50-50 Draw**: The 50-50 draw is a raffle held during a single day at a particular event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the stadium during the event by roaming staff equipped with handheld electronic mobile devices. The gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool. 50% of the prize pool will go to the winner of the random draw which occurs towards the end of the event. The remaining 50% will be set aside for a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n\n3. **Cash Tip Board Raffles**: These are included with the ticket price and offer the chance to win $10,000.", "time_sec": 8.613, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 435, 80535, 975, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 45695, 431, 44090, 95518, 758, 264, 9931, 435, 44090, 11, 13026, 3695, 14403, 448, 5109, 504, 220, 16, 311, 13187, 220, 20, 20, 13, 8886, 11727, 7049, 400, 20, 15, 11, 323, 264, 1965, 315, 220, 17, 15, 7775, 41575, 825, 4583, 11727, 5802, 400, 16, 15, 15, 15, 13, 2619, 525, 1378, 400, 20, 15, 15, 37408, 25, 825, 369, 279, 4124, 11958, 13330, 323, 825, 369, 279, 1156, 11727, 13238, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 20, 15, 12, 20, 15, 11992, 95518, 576, 220, 20, 15, 12, 20, 15, 4038, 374, 264, 435, 44090, 5644, 2337, 264, 3175, 1899, 518, 264, 3953, 1538, 13, 35615, 525, 6088, 311, 51760, 6814, 279, 23889, 2337, 279, 1538, 553, 68253, 5570, 18650, 448, 64949, 14346, 6371, 7611, 13, 576, 19952, 33455, 315, 220, 20, 15, 12, 20, 15, 14403, 6088, 518, 279, 1538, 728, 1119, 264, 21882, 7314, 13, 220, 20, 15, 4, 315, 279, 21882, 7314, 686, 728, 311, 279, 13632, 315, 279, 4194, 4038, 892, 13666, 6974, 279, 835, 315, 279, 1538, 13, 576, 9664, 220, 20, 15, 4, 686, 387, 738, 15663, 369, 264, 47701, 7428, 11882, 553, 279, 34927, 6335, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 47441, 29873, 8751, 431, 80535, 95518, 4220, 525, 5230, 448, 279, 11727, 3349, 323, 3010, 279, 6012, 311, 3164, 400, 16, 15, 11, 15, 15, 15, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1232, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0248, -0.0004, -0.1392, -0.4383, -0.0018, -0.5887, -0.5911, -0.0421, -0.2084, -0.1474, -0.0004, -1.1788, -0.1229, -0.0031, -0.0012, -0.3831, -1.1383, -0.4059, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0065, -0.6691, -0.2877, -0.1956, -0.277, -0.4956, -0.987, -0.0039, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.1953, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.1089, -0.3591, -0.1499, -0.1394, -0.0026, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.7659, -0.0272, -0.3074, -0.311, -0.7693, -0.006, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0759, -0.4239, -0.2265, -0.033, -0.0041, -0.4337, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.0233, -0.0002, -0.0027, -0.0383,