{"id": "523", "question": "temperature for tallahassee florida", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the average high temperature in Tallahassee, Florida is 79 degrees Fahrenheit and the average low is 56 degrees Fahrenheit.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the average high temperature in Tallahassee, Florida is 79 degrees Fahrenheit, and the average low temperature is 56 degrees Fahrenheit. The average weather for Tallahassee, FL - 32310 - 1981-2010 normals is also provided. Additionally, the passage mentions that Tallahassee can experience freezing temperatures sporadically from November to March, with an average of two or three nights dropping to 20 °F (-8 °C) or lower.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the average high temperature in Tallahassee, Florida is 79 degrees Fahrenheit, and the average low temperature is 56 degrees Fahrenheit. The average weather for Tallahassee, FL - 32310 - 1981-2010 normals is also provided. Additionally, the passage mentions that Tallahassee can experience freezing temperatures sporadically from November to March, with an average of two or three nights dropping to 20 °F (-8 °C) or lower.", "time_sec": 3.537, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 5461, 1550, 9315, 304, 41102, 91966, 4060, 11, 9589, 374, 220, 22, 24, 12348, 68723, 11, 323, 279, 5461, 3347, 9315, 374, 220, 20, 21, 12348, 68723, 13, 576, 5461, 9104, 369, 41102, 91966, 4060, 11, 12772, 481, 220, 18, 17, 18, 16, 15, 481, 220, 16, 24, 23, 16, 12, 17, 15, 16, 15, 53452, 374, 1083, 3897, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 21085, 33845, 429, 41102, 91966, 4060, 646, 3139, 42218, 19879, 60916, 329, 2673, 504, 6702, 311, 5470, 11, 448, 458, 5461, 315, 1378, 476, 2326, 21461, 25100, 311, 220, 17, 15, 36286, 37, 10293, 23, 36286, 34, 8, 476, 4722, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.08, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0183, -0.0005, -0.0645, -0.4482, -0.4923, -0.3918, -0.0411, -0.1862, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0708, -0.0043, -0.3285, -0.1955, -0.0057, -0.0003, -0.032, -0.3636, -0.5639, -0.3024, -0.0021, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.3494, -0.0028, -0.0022, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0012, -0.0258, -1.2192, -0.7689, -0.758, -0.9676, -0.0258, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7585, -0.042, -0.8625, -0.004, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.5086, -0.1355, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0143, -1.5794, -1.2172, -0.6276, -0.7735, -1.2321, -0.0, -0.8341, -0.9706, -0.1236, -0.024, -0.409, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5985, -0.4856, -0.6013, -0.0002, -0.0984, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0108, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0557, -0.0153, -0.4612, -0.0001, -0.0102, -0.0639, -0.0626, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.3931, -0.7098, -0.0189, -0.0011, -0.0004, -0.7623, -0.0002, -0.5549, -0.0058, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.0067, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.1525, -0.9993], "cumulative_logprob": -23.9076, "norm_logp": -0.2135, "input_len": 499, "output_tokens": 112, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.9, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows:\n\n1. When a vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on the windshield is read by the antennae.\n2. The E-ZPass account is charged the proper amount as the vehicle passes through the toll lane.\n3. Feedback is provided to the driver on an electronic display.\n4. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies it as a violator, and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows:\n\n1. When a vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on the windshield is read by the antennae.\n2. The E-ZPass account is charged the proper amount as the vehicle passes through the toll lane.\n3. Feedback is provided to the driver on an electronic display.\n4. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies it as a violator, and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.", "time_sec": 3.343, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3197, 264, 7310, 28833, 264, 25851, 2