{"id": "539", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are mentioned in the following passages:\n\n* Passage 1: In the context of the Greenbriar Boys recording the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" with singer Dian James in 1963.\n* Passage 2: As part of a fragmented repetition of the line \"He was a friend of mine\" in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nPassage 1 and Passage 2", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the lyrics \"He was a friend of mine\" are part of a song that was recorded by various artists including the Greenbriar Boys, the Briarwood Singers, Bobby Bare, and Petula Clark. The song was released in 1963 and 1964. The lyrics are repeated multiple times in the song, emphasizing the bond between the singer and the person being referred to as a friend. The song also mentions the friend's death and the singer's sadness over it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the lyrics \"He was a friend of mine\" are part of a song that was recorded by various artists including the Greenbriar Boys, the Briarwood Singers, Bobby Bare, and Petula Clark. The song was released in 1963 and 1964. The lyrics are repeated multiple times in the song, emphasizing the bond between the singer and the person being referred to as a friend. The song also mentions the friend's death and the singer's sadness over it.", "time_sec": 3.727, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 23261, 330, 1519, 572, 264, 4238, 315, 10485, 1, 525, 949, 315, 264, 5492, 429, 572, 12433, 553, 5257, 13511, 2670, 279, 7840, 65, 461, 277, 29757, 11, 279, 54758, 277, 6660, 10833, 388, 11, 37381, 60792, 11, 323, 11333, 5607, 21304, 13, 576, 5492, 572, 5880, 304, 220, 16, 24, 21, 18, 323, 220, 16, 24, 21, 19, 13, 576, 23261, 525, 11504, 5248, 3039, 304, 279,