{"id": "547", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some traits associated with people born in October:\n\n* A keen eye for form and structure (October 14)\n* Success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful (October 1)\n* Restless at heart but craving stability and security (October 5)\n\nIt's important to note that these are generalizations and not necessarily applicable to every individual born in October.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, people born in October have various traits depending on the specific day of the month:\n\n- October 1: Success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful. Best when in control, but can be impatient.\n- October 5: Restless at heart but craves stability and security, leading to hard work.\n\nThese traits are based on Astrology, Numerology, and Cartomancy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, people born in October have various traits depending on the specific day of the month:\n\n- October 1: Success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful. Best when in control, but can be impatient.\n- October 5: Restless at heart but craves stability and security, leading to hard work.\n\nThese traits are based on Astrology, Numerology, and Cartomancy.", "time_sec": 2.761, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1251, 9223, 304, 6527, 614, 5257, 24055, 11649, 389, 279, 3151, 1899, 315, 279, 2254, 1447, 12, 6527, 220, 16, 25, 13047, 35085, 11, 34409, 11, 323, 15726, 7988, 13, 7107, 979, 304, 2524, 11, 714, 646, 387, 73697, 624, 12, 6527, 220, 20, 25, 9063, 1717, 518, 4746, 714, 1560, 4693, 19753, 323, 4763, 11, 6388, 311, 2588, 975, 382, 9485, 24055, 525, 3118, 389, 64129, 35681, 11, 47124, 2449, 11, 323, 13115, 316, 6572, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0635, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0157, -0.0003, -0.0858, -0.0611, -0.0754, -0.0272, -0.001, -0.6631, -1.3681, -0.0602, -0.6524, -0.0001, -0.0671, -0.1436, -0.3988, -0.6287, -0.3191, -0.0123, -1.0287, -0.7137, -1.0102, -0.0004, -0.0412, -0.2932, -1.4548, -0.0018, -0.0006, -0.0021, -0.0003, -0.0603, -0.0108, -0.0002, -0.8899, -1.0427, -0.1527, -0.0336, -0.0001, -0.9599, -1.7129, -0.7393, -0.5419, -0.1236, -1.0177, -0.0043, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.149, -0.0002, -0.5339, -0.0008, -0.0609, -0.0001, -0.3903, -0.1745, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0028, -0.1737, -1.0109, -0.0396, -0.034, -0.0095, -0.8588, -1.3911, -0.0933, -0.0711, -1.1428, -0.0121, -1.0396, -0.0011, -0.0173, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -1.3908, -0.1399], "cumulative_logprob": -25.2249, "norm_logp": -0.3003, "input_len": 459, "output_tokens": 84, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "550", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a transistor is an electronic component made of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier or a switch depending on the flow of electrons through its base. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a small electric current at one end and produces a larger electric current at the other. The flow of electrons is controlled by using a small amount of electricity to turn a valve-like structure in the transistor. In its off state, the holes in the base act as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector. Transistors can have common-emitter configuration where collector current is approximately β times the base current.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a transistor is a miniature electronic component that can function as an amplifier or a switch. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, similar to turning a valve to control a supply of water. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny electric current at one end (an input current) and produces a much bigger electric current (an output current) at the other. Transistors can also work as switches, where the holes in the base act like a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector while the transistor is in its off state. A transistor works when the electrons and the holes start moving across the two junctions between the n-type and p-type silicon.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a transistor is a miniature electronic component that can function as an amplifier or a switch. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, similar to turning a valve to control a supply of water. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny electric current at one end (an input current) and produces a much bigger electric current (an output current) at the other. Transistors can also work as switches, where the holes in the base act like a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector while the transistor is in its off state. A transistor works when the electrons and the holes start moving across the two junctions between the n-type and p-type silicon.", "time_sec": 5.927, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 97941, 374, 264, 56763, 14346, 3692, 429, 646, 729, 438, 458, 60066, 476, 264, 3398, 13, 1084, 4278, 553, 1667, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 17728, 311, 2524, 264, 18126, 389, 264, 1753, 8131, 8149, 315, 17728, 11, 4428, 311, 13054, 264, 31430, 311, 2524, 264, 8149, 315, 3015, 13, 3197, 3238, 438, 458, 60066, 11, 432, 4990, 304, 264, 13673, 9072, 1482, 518, 825, 835, 320, 276, 1946, 1482, 8, 323, 18644, 264, 1753, 11243, 9072, 1482, 320, 276, 2550, 1482, 8, 518, 279, 1008, 13, 4058, 380, 1087, 646, 1083, 975, 438, 31167, 11, 1380, 279, 19766, 304, 279, 2331, 1160, 1075, 264, 22103, 11, 26160, 894, 5089, 1482, 6396, 504, 279, 47263, 311, 279, 31953, 1393, 279, 97941, 374, 304, 1181, 1007, 1584, 13, 362, 97941, 4278, 979, 279, 56578, 323, 279, 19766, 1191, 7218, 3941, 279, 1378, 48241, 82, 1948, 279, 308, 10604, 323, 281, 10604, 50592, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1656, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0147, -0.0004, -0.0597, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0027, -0.0192, -0.6143, -0.0019, -0.0011, -0.1899, -0.1061, -0.4813, -0.1258, -0.6323, -0.0001, -0.0037, -0.0274, -0.0001, -0.0674, -0.5962, -0.9883, -0.0299, -0.4274, -0.0072, -0.0062, -0.05, -0.0, -0.0027, -0.0537, -0.0008, -0.012, -0.0433, -0.0364, -0.0014, -0.2041, -0.0002, -0.0024, -0.0204, -0.0001, -0.1385, -0.6799, -0.0, -0.2537, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0086, -0.0105, -0.1218, -0.1713, -0.0002, -0.000