{"id": "554", "question": "why does the company Oracle have 2 CEOs", "gt": "Oracle has two CEOs because the former CEO, Larry Ellison, stepped down and chose to have two of his co-presidents, Safra Catz and Mark Hurd, share the role of CEO.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Oracle has two CEOs because Larry Ellison, the founder of the company, unexpectedly announced his step down from his CEO post. Ellison named Safra Catz and Mark Hurd, the co-presidents of Oracle, to replace him as CEOs. This decision was made to ensure a smooth transition and to maintain the company's leadership structure.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Oracle has two CEOs because Larry Ellison, the founder of the company, unexpectedly announced his step down from his CEO post. Ellison named Safra Catz and Mark Hurd, the co-presidents of Oracle, to replace him as CEOs. This decision was made to ensure a smooth transition and to maintain the company's leadership structure.", "time_sec": 2.599, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 21422, 702, 1378, 74217, 1576, 29290, 81647, 11, 279, 18996, 315, 279, 2813, 11, 50609, 7228, 806, 3019, 1495, 504, 806, 12156, 1736, 13, 81647, 6941, 12582, 956, 17358, 89, 323, 4389, 472, 16081, 11, 279, 1062, 79776, 6880, 315, 21422, 11, 311, 8290, 1435, 438, 74217, 13, 1096, 5480, 572, 1865, 311, 5978, 264, 10876, 9142, 323, 311, 10306, 279, 2813, 594, 11438, 5944, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.122, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0206, -0.001, -0.0165, -0.1186, -0.2229, -0.578, -0.0024, -0.3928, -0.1816, -0.0001, -0.6697, -0.1281, -0.254, -0.7945, -0.694, -0.0078, -0.0169, -0.719, -0.0255, -0.5677, -0.9523, -0.0096, -0.1284, -0.3529, -0.0753, -0.0818, -0.6213, -1.7399, -0.5542, -0.5617, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2271, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.6027, -0.7843, -0.0931, -0.0032, -0.0002, -0.0313, -0.0025, -0.0067, -0.0712, -0.7022, -0