{"id": "610", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "time_sec": 3.727, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 5100, 21029, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 3060, 1667, 279, 9700, 3811, 438, 697, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1958, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0247, -0.0015, -0.1064, -0.6029, -0.2403, -0.2584, -0.0002, -0.2479, -0.2399, -0.0027, -0.0012, -0.5511, -0.0091, -0.0031, -0.1134, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.2067, -0.0001, -0.005, -0.0269, -0.0013, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.1952, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.1898, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0417, -0.0206, -0.0002, -0.0111, -0.0015, -0.0138, -0.0026, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.3969, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.4505, -0.0008, -0.0014, -0.1032, -0.0128, -0.0103, -0.001, -0.017, -0.0009, -0.0807, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0416, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.042, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.2075, -0.2542, -0.0163, -0.0231, -0.5364, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.1784, -1.0755, -0.0, -0.0591, -0.0041, -0.0057, -0.0028, -0.0, -0.0136, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.5893, -0.6993, -0.3099, -0.0001, -0.1936, -0.3136, -0.0006, -0.0317, -0.0003, -0.0051, -0.0196, -0.0002, -0.0068, -0.0859, -0.0042], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1278, "norm_logp": -0.0904, "input_len": 396, "output_tokens": 101, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "614", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Based on the information given in the passages, to force remove a printer in devices and printers, you need to go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, and then on Printers. Right-click the printer that you want to remove, and click Delete. If it doesn't delete, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete. If your printer is connected to your computer via a USB, disconnect the cable, turn the printer on and off again, and ensure it is in a ready state. If you used Print Manager or Printers folder to remove a printer or printer port, close these applications and stop and restart the Spooler Service.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "time_sec": 3.245, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 10428, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 498, 4157, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 624, 22, 13, 9189, 6452, 438, 28093, 624, 23, 13, 9189, 10428, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2435, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0393, -0.0011, -0.1191, -0.2225, -0.0861, -0.2453, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0215, -0.2399, -0.0002, -0.004, -0.0, -0.3825, -0.1767, -0.0029, -0.0013, -0.51, -0.0651, -0.0003, -0.7628, -0.7116, -0.5244, -0.0001, -0.2188, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.4056, -0.0013, -0.016, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.3919, -0.0078, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.0195, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0359, -0.0, -0.089, -0.0014, -0.5242, -0.0339, -0.0, -0.0081, -0.3971, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.2581, -0.1696, -0.8286, -0.0168, -0.0, -0.0141, -0.7571, -0.4793, -0.0126, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0732, -0.0161, -0.0, -0.0133, -0.0013, -0.3618, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0474, -0.0066, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0133, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0263, -0.0009, -0.7216, -0.0141], "cumulative_logprob": -10.3548, "norm_logp": -0.119, "input_len": 411, "output_tokens": 87, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "616", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "To force removal of a printer in devices and printers:\n1. Use Print Manager or Printers folder to remove the printer or printer port.\n2. Close Print Manager or the Printers folder.\n3. Stop and restart the Spooler Service.\n4. Go to Control Panel > Hardware and Sound > Printers.\n5. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then select Delete.\n6. If the printer is connected to the computer via USB cable, disconnect it from the printer.\n7. Turn off the printer and turn it back on again. Ensure that it is in a ready state.\n8. Remove the printer from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "time_sec": 3.263, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 10428, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 498, 4157, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 624, 22, 13, 9189, 6452, 438, 28093, 624, 23, 13, 9189, 10428, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2435, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0393, -0.0011, -0.1191, -0.2225, -0.0861, -0.2453, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0215, -0.2399, -0.0002, -0.004, -0.0, -0.3825, -0.1767, -0.0029, -0.0013, -0.51, -0.0651, -0.0003, -0.7628, -0.7116, -0.5244, -0.0001, -0.2188, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.4056, -0.0013, -0.016, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.3919, -0.0078, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.0195, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0359, -0.0, -0.089, -0.0014, -0.5242, -0.0339, -0.0, -0.0081, -0.3971, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.2581, -0.1696, -0.8286, -0.0168, -0.0, -0.0141, -0.7571, -0.4793, -0.0126, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0732, -0.0161, -0.0, -0.0133, -0.0013, -0.3618, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0474, -0.0066, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0133, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0263, -0.0009, -0.7216, -0.0141], "cumulative_logprob": -10.3548, "norm_logp": -0.119, "input_len": 411, "output_tokens": 87, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "620", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "pred": "These changes have reshaped the average workplace in America over the past couple of decades, moving away from the traditional office environment of the past.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways:\n\n1. Efficiency and Increased Productivity: The modern workplace has experienced a complete shift in how we spend our time, leading to increased efficiency and productivity.\n\n2. Dynamics of the Workplace: Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed the attitude and processes of the workplace, transforming the environment.\n\n3. Global Interaction: Rapid technological advancement has allowed employees to interact with a global market, enabling them to take work out on the road.\n\nThese changes have reshaped the average workplace in America over the past couple of decades, moving away from the traditional office environment of the past.", "time_sec": 5.314, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 5440, 702, 5497, 279, 26368, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 66567, 323, 61597, 5643, 1927, 25, 576, 6481, 26368, 702, 10321, 264, 4583, 6407, 304, 1246, 582, 8329, 1039, 882, 11, 6388, 311, 7172, 15024, 323, 25