{"id": "635", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the key similarities and differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters and hormones) to transmit signals.\n* Both systems have negative feedback mechanisms to regulate their function.\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of glands.\n* Transmission of signals occurs through electrical impulses in the nervous system, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n* The nervous system has a continuous structure, with cells connected to each other, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs not physically connected to each other.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to transmit signals.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\n\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\n\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\n\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "time_sec": 6.433, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 785, 11799, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "l