{"id": "641", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "time_sec": 7.824, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 624, 18, 13, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 614, 2779, 78248, 323, 9503, 98605, 10530, 624, 785, 11799, 1948, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 510, 16, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 17, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 323, 6777, 2513, 1741, 438, 23552, 6814, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 18, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 1730, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 1730, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 323, 646, 387, 11691, 553, 6543, 504, 825, 949, 311, 2441, 949, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1802, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0151, -0.0003, -0.1825, -0.4456, -0.3014, -0.0435, -0.0006, -0.3537, -0.