{"id": "652", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine can indicate various things. Here's what we can infer from the passages:\n\n* Red urine (passage 1) indicates the presence of blood in the urine, which can be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer.\n* Deep purple urine (passage 2) is associated with porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Certain foods and medications can also change urine color.\n* The normal color of urine is pale yellow (passage 3), but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is the meaning of different colors of urine?\" based on these passages is:\n\nRed urine can indicate the presence of blood in the urine, while deep purple urine is associated with porphyria. Changes in urine color can also be caused by kidney diseases.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine can vary due to several factors. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning. Additionally, certain foods and medications, such as beets, berries, and fava beans, can change the color of urine. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Lastly, red urine can be a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer and warrants a visit to a doctor or urologist.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine can vary due to several factors. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning. Additionally, certain foods and medications, such as beets, berries, and fava beans, can change the color of urine. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Lastly, red urine can be a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer and warrants a visit to a doctor or urologist.", "time_sec": 4.915, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 4152, 311, 3807, 9363, 13, 576, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 1894, 646, 387, 28752, 304, 5048, 315, 37942, 18808, 1380, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 525, 71187, 287, 13, 22406, 11, 3654, 15298, 323, 29910, 11, 1741, 438, 387, 1415, 11, 62394, 11, 323, 282, 2907, 26896, 11, 646, 2297, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 13, 18183, 24932, 39235, 374, 458, 24588, 28583, 315, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 264, 8848, 11, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 70709, 11, 2518, 39235, 646, 387, 264, 1841, 315, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 892, 646, 13216, 6001, 4682, 1075, 28920, 476, 9387, 323, 54588, 264, 3947, 311, 264, 10668, 476, 575, 299, 839, 380, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2522, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0284, -0.0008, -0.0872, -0.0903, -0.3502, -0.0026, -0.0163, -0.2047, -0.5606, -1.4594, -0.0, -0.9441, -0.1162, -0.9272, -1.4129, -0.1653, -0.0195, -0.1837, -0.0018, -0.0165, -0.2936, -0.0002, -0.1996, -0.4387, -0.0489, -0.594, -0.0, -0.026, -0.0008, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.3994, -0.0006, -0.6248, -0.6157, -0.0243, -0.5047, -0.3099, -0.6608, -0.5934, -0.0128, -0.013, -0.0137, -0.5649, -0.044, -0.0038, -0.001, -0.0169, -0.0008, -0.0347, -0.0, -0.0039, -0.0134, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0