, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "662", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "pred": "4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\n\n1. To improve the skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture can also be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\n\n2. To clean ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\n\n3. To repel fleas: Spray the dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas. Additionally, a flea comb can be used to remove fleas after spraying the coat.\n\n4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "time_sec": 7.605, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 25, 19219, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 253