{"id": "666", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "When you breathe in, your diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, expanding the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract to expand the ribcage. Pressure inside the chest is reduced, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. On the other hand, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. Air rich in carbon dioxide is then forced out of the lungs and windpipe. Breathing out does not require any effort from your body unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity.", "pred": "When you breathe out (expiration), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when you breathe in (inspiration), the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs.\n\nWhen you breathe out (expiration), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "time_sec": 4.176, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 498, 36297, 304, 320, 1330, 28479, 701, 279, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 5116, 11, 23175, 279, 20131, 66, 424, 13, 576, 1853, 94796, 76, 17080, 11, 22266, 91270, 311, 5263, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 15138, 13, 38990, 4766, 279, 15138, 374, 38820, 11, 323, 3720, 374, 52212, 1119, 279, 44174, 382, 4498, 498, 36297, 700, 320, 63643, 701, 279, 1853, 94796, 76, 11967, 288, 323, 10797, 39772, 1119, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 576, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 1948, 279, 55149, 1083, 11967, 311, 7949, 279, 3550, 304, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 1634, 279, 3550, 304, 279, 15138, 55329, 5221, 9155, 11, 3720, 9080, 304, 12499, 39489, 374, 9575, 700, 315, 697, 44174, 323, 9956, 13768, 11, 323, 1221, 700, 315, 697, 19142, 476, 10780, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3306, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.2968, -0.1132, -0.0316, -0.2472, -0.2611, -0.4508, -1.1247, -0.0923, -0.5616, -0.1202, -0.4396, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0143, -0.0201, -0.0926, -0.0009, -0.0008, -0.0068, -0.0, -0.6883, -0.1386, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3903, -0.0194, -0.0078, -0.0158, -0.0093, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.2291, -0.3384, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0174, -0.0043, -0.202, -0.1798, -0.0027, -0.0019, -0.0551, -0.0003, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.6182, -0.0167, -0.0031, -0.0117, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.2573, -0.0014, -0.3548, -0.2142, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0089, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.0048, -0.0646, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.1605, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1842, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0044, -0.0007, -0.2567, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0061, -0.0084, -0.0024, -0.0168, -0.003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0034, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0066, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0549, -0.0, -0.0765, -0.0073, -0.0, -0.0051, -0.0031, -0.0046, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.09, -0.4973], "cumulative_logprob": -9.4805, "norm_logp": -0.0713, "input_len": 461, "output_tokens": 133, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "668", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is what happens when you breathe in and out:\n\nWhen you breathe in (inhalation):\n\n* The intercostal muscles contract, causing the ribcage to expand.\n* The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest.\n* Pressure inside the chest is lowered, allowing air to be sucked into the lungs.\n\nWhen you breathe out (exhalation):\n\n* The diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity.\n* The intercostal muscles relax, reducing the space in the chest cavity.\n* Air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of the lungs and windpipe, and then out of the nose or mouth.\n\nSo, in summary, when you breathe in, the diaphragm and intercostal muscles contract to bring air into the lungs, and when you breathe out, the diaphragm and intercostal muscles relax to force air out of the lungs.", "pred": "When you breathe out (expiration), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when you breathe in (inspiration), the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs.\n\nWhen you breathe out (expiration), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "time_sec": 4.093, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 498, 36297, 304, 320, 1330, 28479, 701, 279, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 5116, 11, 23175, 279, 20131, 66, 424, 13, 576, 1853, 94796, 76, 17080, 11, 22266, 91270, 311, 5263, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 15138, 13, 38990, 4766, 279, 15138, 374, 38820, 11, 323, 3720, 374, 52212, 1119, 279, 44174, 382, 4498, 498, 36297, 700, 320, 63643, 701, 279, 1853, 94796, 76, 11967, 288, 323, 10797, 39772, 1119, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 576, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 1948, 279, 55149, 1083, 11967, 311, 7949, 279, 3550, 304, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 1634, 279, 3550, 304, 279, 15138, 55329, 5221, 9155, 11, 3720, 9080, 304, 12499, 39489, 374, 9575, 700, 315, 697, 44174, 323, 9956, 13768, 11, 323, 1221, 700, 315, 697, 19142, 476, 10780, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3306, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.2968, -0.1132, -0.0316, -0.2472, -0.2611, -0.4508, -1.1247, -0.0923, -0.5616, -0.1202, -0.4396, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0143, -0.0201, -0.0926, -0.0009, -0.0008, -0.0068, -0.0, -0.6883, -0.1386, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3903, -0.0194, -0.0078, -0.0158, -0.0093, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.2291, -0.3384, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0174, -0.0043, -0.202, -0.1798, -0.0027, -0.0019, -0.0551, -0.0003, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.6182, -0.0167, -0.0031, -0.0117, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.2573, -0.0014, -0.3548, -0.2142, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0089, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.0048, -0.0646, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.1605, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1842, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0044, -0.0007, -0.2567, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0061, -0.0084, -0.0024, -0.0168, -0.003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0034, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0066, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0549, -0.0, -0.0765, -0.0073, -0.0, -0.0051, -0.0031, -0.0046, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.09, -0.4973], "cumulative_logprob": -9.4805, "norm_logp": -0.0713, "