{"id": "691", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "gt": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The score is primarily based on the number of snaps sent and received.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "time_sec": 1.724, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 55179, 5456, 13, 576, 46769, 6286, 429, 279, 5456, 374, 264, 2629, 315, 279, 1372, 315, 51304, 3208, 323, 51304, 3949, 11, 323, 1052, 374, 902, 27039, 429, 10099, 7343, 42972, 311, 419, 5456, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2988, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0478, -0.0014, -0.0191, -0.1069, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.022, -0.0069, -0.2654, -0.5487, -0.5789, -0.0005, -0.0227, -0.2342, -0.8719, -1.4827, -0.1677, -0.6467, -0.2407, -0.0228, -0.8715, -0.0116, -0.0002, -0.0129, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0031, -0.0134, -0.0003, -0.209, -0.0, -0.3981, -0.3194, -0.9232, -0.0387, -0.0032, -0.4292, -0.0171, -0.5258, -0.0213, -0.4007, -0.0005, -1.1539, -0.8797, -0.0137, -0.1439], "cumulative_logprob": -11.9797, "norm_logp": -0.2445, "input_len": 564, "output_tokens": 49, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "694", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is increased by sending and receiving more snaps, and by interacting with friends on the platform. Watching stories is not mentioned as a factor that contributes to increasing one's score. Therefore, the answer to the question is: No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "time_sec": 1.495, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 55179, 5456, 13, 576, 46769, 6286, 429, 279, 5456, 374, 264, 2629, 315, 279, 1372, 315, 51304, 3208, 323, 51304, 3949, 11, 323, 1052, 374, 902, 27039, 429, 10099, 7343, 42972, 311, 419, 5456, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2988, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0478, -0.0014, -0.0191, -0.1069, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.022, -0.0069, -0.2654, -0.5487, -0.5789, -0.0005, -0.0227, -0.2342, -0.8719, -1.4827, -0.1677, -0.6467, -0.2407, -0.0228, -0.8715, -0.0116, -0.0002, -0.0129, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0031, -0.0134, -0.0003, -0.209, -0.0, -0.3981, -0.3194, -0.9232, -0.0387, -0.0032, -0.4292, -0.0171, -0.5258, -0.0213, -0.4007, -0.0005, -1.1539, -0.8797, -0.0137, -0.1439], "cumulative_logprob": -11.9797, "norm_logp": -0.2445, "input_len": 564, "output_tokens": 49, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "696", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\n\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\n\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "time_sec": 7.847, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 279, 11116, 421, 498, 1366, 803, 382, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19187, 848, 11, 23065, 3786, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 19, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 13, 910, 399, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1423, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0192, -0.0007, -0.1253, -0.8282, -0.5741, -0.1317, -0.5772, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.1355, -0.0217, -0.0026, -1.68, -0.227, -1.1069, -0.3794, -0.6575, -0.0004, -0.3007, -0.3985, -1.9093, -0.5729, -0.0531, -0.7733, -0.4329, -0.6147, -0.0, -0.0278, -0.2838, -0.2766, -0.6861, -0.0021, -0.3951, -0.0006, -1.2885, -0.0657, -0.0333, -0.9146, -0.0009, -0.0039, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0001, -0.0244, -0.1439, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0024, -0.001, -0.9609, -1.2432, -0.3579, -1.2167, -0.6695, -0.0069, -0.0, -0.0267, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.1687, -0.2034, -0.7871, -0.253, -0.0094, -0.6479, -0.0873, -0.1017, -0.0437, -0.4074, -0.0839, -0.3831, -0.0021, -0.0001, -1.6464, -0.7504, -0.1351, -0.0, -0.2026, -0.0591, -0.238, -0.0324, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0677, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0862, -0.002, -0.0001, -0.1266, -0.0185, -0.4955, -0.2064, -0.1633, -0.049, -0.1644, -0.0101, -0.4832, -0.0014, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0078, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0089, -0.4362, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2009, -0.0002, -0.7619, -0.0022, -0.0282, -0.0006, -0.0308, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2539, -0.0326, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.9055, -0.6081, -0.0215, -0.3394, -0.0036, -0.5158, -0.1657, -0.0001, -0.3294, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.4094, -0.0081, -0.0, -0.7117, -0.0936, -0.2829, -0.2497, -0.0, -0.0987, -0.0011, -0.0258, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.7445, -0.7263, -0.5459, -0.0008, -0.0005, -0.2931, -0.2032, -0.0001, -0.6396, -0.0, -0.01, -0.0035, -0.0076, -0.0207, -0.3181, -0.1008, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0054, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0691, -0.001, -0.0, -0.6032, -0.0105, -0.0048, -0.0, -0.0331, -0.0173, -0.0001, -0.0238, -0.7883, -0.1803, -0.0017, -0.3004, -0.274, -0.042, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0505, -0.0004, -0.1163, -0.0098, -0.0, -0.2269, -0.1235, -0.027, -0.0027, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0638, -0.0067, -0.0, -0.0099, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.5602, -0.0224], "cumulative_logprob": -42.1595, "norm_logp": -0.1882, "input_len": 439, "output_tokens": 224, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "698", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\n\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\n\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "time_sec": 7.678, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 279, 11116, 421, 498, 1366, 803, 382, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19187, 848, 11, 23065, 3786, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 18, 13, 2320