{"id": "705", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "pred": "1. Gross motor skills: Children run through sprinklers, fill and pour water, and engage in physical activities that enhance their gross motor skills.\n2. Academic learning: Water play helps with science by teaching concepts like floating and sinking, and with math by practicing measuring and comparing quantities of water.\n3. Creativity: Children use their imagination and pretend while playing with water, fostering creative thinking and expression.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, children learn several things with water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Children run through sprinklers, fill and pour water, and engage in physical activities that enhance their gross motor skills.\n2. Academic learning: Water play helps with science by teaching concepts like floating and sinking, and with math by practicing measuring and comparing quantities of water.\n3. Creativity: Children use their imagination and pretend while playing with water, fostering creative thinking and expression.", "time_sec": 3.133, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2841, 3960, 3807, 2513, 448, 3015, 1486, 1447, 16, 13, 42807, 8872, 7361, 25, 15044, 1598