{"id": "716", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, the following exercises are mentioned as toning the chest:\n\n* Modified tri-set for the chest (not specified)\n* Pushups\n* Dumbbell bench presses\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What exercises tone the chest?\" based on the given passages is:\n\nModified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and dumbbell bench presses.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, exercises that tone the chest include modified tri-sets for the chest and pairing pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, exercises that tone the chest include modified tri-sets for the chest and pairing pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.", "time_sec": 0.982, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 22932, 429, 16232, 279, 15138, 2924, 10807, 2406, 12, 4917, 369, 279, 15138, 323, 47713, 4484, 8602, 448, 1602, 8811, 7289, 315, 29255, 17250, 13425, 52963, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0934, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0223, -0.0012, -0.0384, -0.8352, -0.0745, -0.0044, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0121, -1.245, -0.0018, -0.0508, -0.0001, -0.4587, -0.0072, -0.0, -0.4944, -0.2626, -0.0012, -0.0901, -0.0001, -0.0796, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0488, -0.8], "cumulative_logprob": -4.6256, "norm_logp": -0.136, "input_len": 416, "output_tokens": 34, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "719", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "time_sec": 5.456, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3460, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 54945, 458, 18636, 323, 29273, 14983, 432, 1119, 279, 52925, 3193, 11829, 7509, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 18636, 594, 379, 22604, 624, 18, 13, 13001, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 304, 279, 49837, 3015, 11, 22573, 279, 7509, 26558, 48585, 323, 902, 3015, 5221, 1119, 279, 7509, 624, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 26334, 323, 1077, 279, 18636, 4296, 369, 4743, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 26334, 323, 990, 264, 3460, 1739, 15521, 45505, 476, 259, 13181, 311, 11893, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 700, 315, 279, 4017, 3015, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 35841, 1495, 916, 264, 11968, 323, 29273, 3493, 389, 279, 5622, 311, 4879, 279, 3193, 3854, 18636, 8630, 279, 11968, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2856, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1295, -0.0014, -0.1497, -0.4931, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0115, -0.1625, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.9875, -0.0365, -0.0025, -0.0146, -0.6041, -0.0015, -0.0001, -0.5311, -0.0007, -0.0023, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0006, -0.03, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.1299, -0.0566, -0.0, -0.118, -0.007, -0.0004, -0.5232, -0.0002, -0.4981, -0.1393, -0.1701, -0.0079, -0.0026, -0.1232, -0.3061, -0.0019, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0006, -0.2817, -0.0141, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0097, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.3682, -0.0, -0.0283, -0.0034, -0.0004, -0.0094, -0.0027, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0093, -0.5766, -0.2562, -0.0003, -0.0061, -0.0, -0.0189, -0.0334, -0.0, -0.0156, -0.0035, -0.2014, -0.0002, -0.0088, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.012, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0005, -0.4288, -0.0, -0.0888, -0.0033, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0069, -0.134, -0.0001, -0.0131, -0.