{"id": "731", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the breathing process involves the contraction and relaxation of various muscles, including the diaphragm muscle, to move air in and out of the lungs. This process involves an exchange of gases between the body and the external environment, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity by contracting the muscles involved in breathing draws air into the lungs, causing them to expand and decreasing air pressure below atmospheric pressure. Therefore, the passage does not mention any specific step involved in processing air before it reaches the lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "time_sec": 3.537, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 4990, 4126, 6430, 304, 46494, 36371, 1182, 10158, 7468, 476, 6849, 20239, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1144, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0192, -0.0017, -0.0513, -0.1644, -0.4432, -0.0276, -0.1768, -0.2806, -0.1617, -0.0689, -0.0005, -0.0033, -0.184, -0.2456, -0.5775, -0.0006, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2787, -0.6329, -0.5335, -0.8774, -0.2622, -0.0028, -0.0768, -0.0185, -0.6455, -0.6592, -0.0252, -0.7041, -0.0748, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.4812, -0.476, -0.7771, -0.9495, -0.055, -0.3052, -0.0003, -0.0816, -0.0031, -0.1079, -0.1036, -0.4615, -0.2492, -0.0038, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0028, -0.3327, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.01, -0.0, -0.0381, -0.0014, -0.0465, -0.0006, -0.0013, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0367, -0.1281, -0.8912, -0.0, -0.1431, -0.3663, -0.1573, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.109, -0.0004, -0.0017, -0.0047, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.1282, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0369, -0.7194, -0.3621, -0.0026, -0.3171, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.112, -0.1336, -0.4553, -0.0046, -0.3135, -0.0214, -0.2658, -0.486, -0.0058, -0.0, -0.4037, -0.1219, -0.0046, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0465, -0.3819], "cumulative_logprob": -17.9781, "norm_logp": -0.1634, "input_len": 512, "output_tokens": 110, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 4.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "733", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs:\n\nWhen you inhale, the diaphragm muscle contracts, moving down from the bottom of your rib cage towards your abdominal region, which causes the thoracic cavity to increase in volume. This decrease in air pressure in the lungs below atmospheric pressure forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing you to inhale.\n\nTherefore, the air you breathe is processed by the diaphragm muscle before it reaches your lungs, which contracts to take air into the lungs and relax to let it out again. Additionally, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, such as oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment, which occurs in the lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "time_sec": 3.603, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 4990, 4126, 6430, 304, 46494, 36371, 1182, 10158, 7468, 476, 6849, 20239, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1144, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0192, -0.0017, -0.0513, -0.1644, -0.4432, -0.0276, -0.1768, -0.2806, -0.1617, -0.0689, -0.0005, -0.0033, -0.184, -0.2456, -0.5775, -0.0006, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2787, -0.6329, -0.5335, -0.8774, -0.2622, -0.0028, -0.0768, -0.0185, -0.6455, -0.6592, -0.0252, -0.7041, -0.0748, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.4812, -0.476, -0.7771, -0.9495, -0.055, -0.3052, -0.0003, -0.0816, -0.0031, -0.1079, -0.1036, -0.4615, -0.2492, -0.0038, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0028, -0.3327, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.01, -0.0, -0.0381, -0.0014, -0.0465, -0.0006, -0.0013, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0367, -0.1281, -0.8912, -0.0, -0.1431, -0.3663, -0.1573, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.109, -0.0004, -0.0017, -0.0047, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.1282, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0369, -0.7194, -0.3621, -0.0026, -0.3171, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.112, -0.1336, -0.4553, -0.0046, -0.3135, -0.0214, -0.2658, -0.486, -0.0058, -0.0, -0.4037, -0.1219, -0.0046, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0465, -0.3819], "cumulative_logprob": -17.9781, "norm_logp": -0.1634, "input_len": 512, "output_tokens": 110, "eval_metrics": {"