{"id": "21", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.", "time_sec": 4.28, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 13, 2379, 525, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 8, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 6879, 84786, 25351, 4271, 35595, 2820, 3516, 525, 12600, 311, 12989, 33029, 65366, 273, 288, 11, 69120, 448, 3613, 11, 12565, 11, 323, 38110, 311, 7269, 279, 8084, 2820, 323, 1632, 32751, 315, 11214, 5380, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2025, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0451, -0.0007, -0.0993, -0.0212, -0.0, -0.0095, -0.0001, -0.9821, -0.3989, -0.366, -0.5643, -0.0871, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.8652, -0.0028, -0.4329, -0.5939, -0.7531, -0.5912, -0.0191, -0.0072, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0589, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0502, -0.1118, -0.0032, -0.0035, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0045, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.4917, -0.4327, -0.3325, -0.0365, -0.0, -0.0365, -0.1804, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0107, -0.7303, -0.0, -0.9731, -0.0571, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0884, -0.0004, -0.0048, -0.0717, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.9692, -0.0503, -0.0001, -0.0171, -0.0026, -0.0003, -0.0205, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0489, -0.3173, -0.4481, -0.0128, -0.0027, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0354, -1.1085], "cumulative_logprob": -12.7646, "norm_logp": -0.1316, "input_len": 467, "output_tokens": 97, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "24", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nMagellan of Virginia does offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses. According to passage 1, Magellan is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\n\nAdditionally, Magellan of Virginia has been selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. This is mentioned in passage 2.\n\nFinally, Magellan of Virginia offers a Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for providers to address their questions and issues. This is mentioned in passage 3.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.", "time_sec": 4.01, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 13, 2379, 525, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 8, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 6879, 84786, 25351, 4271, 35595, 2820, 3516, 525, 12600, 311, 12989, 33029, 65366, 273, 288, 11, 69120, 448, 3613, 11, 12565, 11, 323, 38110, 311, 7269, 279, 8084, 2820, 323, 1632, 32751, 315, 11214, 5380, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2025, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0451, -0.0007, -0.0993, -0.0212, -0.0, -0.0095, -0.0001, -0.9821, -0.3989, -0.366, -0.5643, -0.0871, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.8652, -0.0028, -0.4329, -0.5939, -0.7531, -0.5912, -0.0191, -0.0072, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0589, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0502, -0.1118, -0.0032, -0.0035, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0045, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.4917, -0.4327, -0.3325, -0.0365, -0.0, -0.0365, -0.1804, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0107, -0.7303, -0.0, -0.9731, -0.0571, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0884, -0.0004, -0.0048, -0.0717, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.9692, -0.0503, -0.0001, -0.0171, -0.0026, -0.0003, -0.0205, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0489, -0.3173, -0.4481, -0.0128, -0.0027, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0354, -1.1085], "cumulative_logprob": -12.7646, "norm_logp": -0.1316, "input_len": 467, "output_tokens": 97, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "time_sec": 7.307, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1445, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0243, -0.0012, -0.0912, -0.3399, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0028, -0.0053, -0.0005, -0.2095, -0.5903, -0.0032, -0.0009, -0.4005, -0.0027, -0.0001, -0.7206, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0305, -0.0008, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.2991, -0.0309, -0.0174, -0.0528, -0.0381, -0.0059, -0.1396, -0.0179, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.1738, -0.004, -0.0, -0.2866, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0016, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.437, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.001, -0.0014, -0.0337, -0.0005, -0.0164, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0288, -0.0061, -0.0797, -0.1202, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0092, -0.0087, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0125, -0.0113, 