{"id": "30", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\nPassage 1 provides tips on how to repair stuck or frozen door locks, keys that don’t work, and latches that don’t latch. However, it does not specifically address the issue of a door that won't lock.\n\nPassage 2 provides instructions on how to fix a door that won't shut or lock properly by removing the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and aligning it back on. This method might work for doors that won't lock due to a misaligned door stop.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional troubleshooting steps for when a door latch won't catch due to misalignment with the strike plate. This passage suggests enlarging the latch hole in the jamb, tightening the hinges, and moving the strike plate to align with the latch.\n\nIn summary, there is no definitive solution in the provided passages to fix a door that won't lock directly. However, these passages provide general tips and troubleshooting steps that may help identify and resolve related issues such as misaligned door stops or latches. If the problem persists after trying these methods, it may be best to consult a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "time_sec": 7.001, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1445, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0243, -0.0012, -0.0912, -0.3399, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0028, -0.0053, -0.0005, -0.2095, -0.5903, -0.0032, -0.0009, -0.4005, -0.0027, -0.0001, -0.7206, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0305, -0.0008, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.2991, -0.0309, -0.0174, -0.0528, -0.0381, -0.0059, -0.1396, 