{"id": "36", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\nPassage 1:\n\n* Spray a baking sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n* Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 2:\n\n* Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Bake the fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n* Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n* Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\n* Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\n\nTherefore, to cook pollock, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n2. Place the fillets on a baking sheet or in the oven.\n3. Cook the pollock until it flakes easily, either by baking it in the oven or on the stovetop.\n4. Add cheese to the pollock if desired and return it to the oven to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "time_sec": 4.669, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0931, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0132, -0.0003, -0.1448, -0.5922, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.774, -0.1409, -0.0029, -0.0039, -0.7216, -0.0037, -0.0015, -0.0958, -0.0001, -0.1464, -0.0002, -0.0025, -0.002, -0.0021, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.1437, -0.0042, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0449, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0472, -0.004, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0022, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0141, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.6371, -0.3162, -0.5859, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0117, -0.0138, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0103, -0.2117, -0.4999, -0.0018, -0.0063, -0.9027, -0.1814, -0.0003, -0.0151, -0.3546, -0.3567, -0.0209, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.5569, -0.0465, -0.0001, -0.8216, -0.0298, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7481, -0.0051, -0.0298, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0017, -0.0033, -0.0285, -0.0, -0.0049, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0099, -0.0003, -0.6631, -0.0092, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0525, -0.1226, -0.0015, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.1312, -0.6289, -0.0962, -0.0103, -0.0052, -0.0001, -0.0187, -0.1489, -0.0033], "cumulative_logprob": -11.3173, "norm_logp": -0.0951, "input_len": 415, "output_tokens": 119, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "38", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "time_sec": 4.808, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0931, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0132, -0.0003, -0.1448, -0.5922, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.774, -0.1409, -0.0029, -0.0039, -0.7216, -0.0037, -0.0015, -0.0958, -0.0001, -0.1464, -0.0002, -0.0025, -0.002, -0.0021, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.1437, -0.0042, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0449, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0472, -0.004, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0022, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0141, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.6371, -0.3162, -0.5859, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0117, -0.0138, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0103, -0.2117, -0.4999, -0.0018, -0.0063, -0.9027, -0.1814, -0.0003, -0.0151, -0.3546, -0.3567, -0.0209, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.5569, -0.0465, -0.0001, -0.8216, -0.0298, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7481, -0.0051, -0.0298, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0017, -0.0033, -0.0285, -0.0, -0.0049, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0099, -0.0003, -0.6631, -0.0092, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0525, -0.1226, -0.0015, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.1312, -0.6289, -0.0962, -0.0103, -0.0052, -0.0001, -0.0187, -0.1489, -0.0033], "cumulative_logprob": -11.3173, "norm_logp": -0.0951, "input_len": 415, "output_tokens": 119, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "40", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "time_sec": 9.785, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 432, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 498, 525, 11889, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498