{"id": "64", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "gt": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is either by separating the blue field from the flag and burning it in a peaceful manner before burying the ashes, or by conducting a proper ceremony where the flag is folded in the customary triangle fold and then burned.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "time_sec": 1.242, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 13, 576, 5181, 1969, 387, 47035, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2479, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0138, -0.0012, -0.0117, -0.0276, -0.0022, -0.0237, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.208, -0.0004, -0.2794, -0.3135, -0.3522, -0.2816, -0.2781, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.0023, -0.0006, -0.2363, -0.9731, -0.0562, -0.0718, -0.0023, -0.0042, -0.0028, -0.0014, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.3146, -0.2191], "cumulative_logprob": -3.9342, "norm_logp": -0.1035, "input_len": 394, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "67", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to either:\n\n1. Burn it in a peaceful manner, removing the blue field first and burying the ashes, or\n2. Perform a proper ceremony by folding the flag in a triangle fold before burning it.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: \"Option 1 or Option 2.\"", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "time_sec": 1.618, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 13, 576, 5181, 1969, 387, 47035, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2479, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0138, -0.0012, -0.0117, -0.0276, -0.0022, -0.0237, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.208, -0.0004, -0.2794, -0.3135, -0.3522, -0.2816, -0.2781, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.0023, -0.0006, -0.2363, -0.9731, -0.0562, -0.0718, -0.0023, -0.0042, -0.0028, -0.0014, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.3146, -0.2191], "cumulative_logprob": -3.9342, "norm_logp": -0.1035, "input_len": 394, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "73", "question": "how to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you:\n\n1. Physical contact: Avoid physical contact that could be misinterpreted as fondling or sexual activity (Passage 1).\n2. Eye contact: If your coworker is consistently staring at you, it may be a sign that they are interested in you (Passage 2).\n3. Smiling: If your coworker smiles at you excessively, even when there is no apparent reason to do so, it may be a sign of flirtation (Passage 2).\n4. Seeking contact: If your coworker consistently finds reasons to be near you or seek you out discreetly, it may indicate that they have feelings for you (Passage 3).\n\nHowever, it is essential to remember that these signs alone do not necessarily mean that your coworker is interested in you romantically. It's important to pay attention to the context of their behavior and communicate openly to avoid misunderstandings.\n\nIf you are unsure about your coworker's intentions, it may be best to avoid physical contact and observe their behavior over time before making any conclusions. Additionally, it's crucial to respect your coworker's boundaries and maintain a professional work environment.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs such as:\n1. Physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\n2. If the coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so.\n3. If the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.\n4. If the coworker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\n5. If the coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you.\n6. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admiration.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs such as:\n1. Physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\n2. If the coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so.\n3. If the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.\n4. If the coworker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\n5. If the coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you.\n6. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admiration.", "time_sec": 6.19, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3291, 421, 697, 8593, 59968, 261, 374, 87242, 448, 498, 11, 1401, 369, 11929, 1741, 438, 510, 16, 13, 27379, 3645, 429, 655, 28146, 311, 7244, 5702, 476, 646, 387, 29671, 495, 3260, 438, 21208, 2718, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 4977, 28113, 476, 13230, 429, 498, 537, 3060, 87242, 448, 1435, 11, 653, 773, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 13719, 894, 2874, 311, 5796, 498, 11, 432, 374, 264, 1841, 315, 87242, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 2677, 42532, 518, 498, 518, 975, 979, 1052, 374, 902, 1661, 2874, 369, 432, 11, 1340, 1231, 1075, 498, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 374, 14971, 518, 697, 18010, 323, 10887, 498, 700, 61404, 398, 11, 432, 594, 264, 15440, 429, 279, 1697, 13151, 498, 624, 21, 13, 42797, 894, 2874, 311, 614, 3645, 448, 498, 374, 458, 8036, 1841, 315, 36705, 476, 65839, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1499, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0282, -0.0015, -0.1228, -0.5623, -0.1146, -0.0, -0.0301, -0.0005, -0.0053, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.1868, -0.8803, -0.0186, -0.4313, -0.2841, -0.0002, -1.4534, -0.0716, -0.0017, -1.0727, -0.0739, -0.1713, -1.6956, -0.00