{"id": "78", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\nStep 1: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n\nStep 2: Lightly oil the grate.\n\nStep 3: Combine beer and onions in a large pot, bring to a boil, and submerge the bratwurst. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n\nStep 4: Simmer the bratwurst in the beer mixture for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n\nStep 5: Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and grill it on the preheated grill for an additional 5 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until browned and cooked through.\n\nStep 6: Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side dish.\n\nNote: It's important to prick the bratwurst with a fork before cooking to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Also, cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "time_sec": 7.349, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 624, 20, 13, 2691, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 311, 279, 3338, 624, 21, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 16, 15, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0998, -0.0, -0.0, -0.027, -0.0003, -0.2464, -0.5368, -0.4662, -0.0873, -0.0015, -0.0006, -0.0022, -0.0383, -0.1164, -0.0123, -0.0038, -0.6988, -0.0002, -0.1124, -0.0016, -0.0005, -0.0442, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.524, -0.0062, -0.0001, -0.705, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.015, -0.3002, -0.0081, -0.0116, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.9509, -0.5693, -0.2424, -0.1832, -0.0078, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0081, -0.0069, -0.3906, -0.0068, -0.0097, -0.0004, -0.0008, -0.0244, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.1423, -0.0003, -0.0015, -0.0042, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0