{"id": "96", "question": "typical weather in indiana", "gt": "The typical weather in Indiana is characterized by long, warm, humid, and wet summers. The winters are chilly and windy with some snowfall. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F and is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F. The state also experiences some rainfall, with the wettest year recording 57.65 inches of rain and the driest 24.97 inches. The most snowfall recorded in a season was 74.5 inches.", "pred": "1. Summers are long, warm, humid, and wet.\n2. Winters are chilly and windy.\n3. It is partly cloudy year-round.\n4. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F.\n5. The temperature is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F.\n6. The wettest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of measured rain.\n7. The driest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1934 with 24.97 inches of measured rain.\n8. The most snowfall recorded in Rockford was 74.5 inches in one season.\n9. The maximum monthly precipitation was over 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes:\n\n1. Summers are long, warm, humid, and wet.\n2. Winters are chilly and windy.\n3. It is partly cloudy year-round.\n4. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F.\n5. The temperature is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F.\n6. The wettest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of measured rain.\n7. The driest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1934 with 24.97 inches of measured rain.\n8. The most snowfall recorded in Rockford was 74.5 inches in one season.\n9. The maximum monthly precipitation was over 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "time_sec": 6.045, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 14260, 9104, 304, 21591, 5646, 1447, 16, 13, 79648, 525, 1293, 11, 8205, 11, 65938, 11, 323