{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "time_sec": 2.814, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 82316, 323, 17188, 389, 1817, 1008, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 30201, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0332, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0133, -0.0003, -0.0416, -0.3297, -0.1633, -0.0061, -0.0024, -0.0135, -1.0133, -1.391, -0.2251, -1.0208, -0.1708, -0.378, -0.176, -0.5443, -0.0707, -0.0031, -0.0587, -0.2583, -0.6373, -0.2016, -0.098, -0.0063, -0.5936, -0.0099, -0.5695, -0.2615, -0.0087, -0.0078, -0.6665, -0.0049, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0716, -0.0, -0.1811, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.5634, -0.6693, -0.042, -0.0, -0.1682, -0.0009, -0.181, -0.0015, -0.0035, -0.0001, -0.0252, -0.0261, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0195, -0.2964, -0.0413, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0078, -0.0088, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0314, -1.3035, -0.5778, -1.0791, -0.4067, -0.3662, -1.1669, -0.0003, -0.1036, -0.0002, -0.1203, -0.0844, -0.638, -0.1205, -0.0031, -0.2409, -0.5585, -0.0251, -0.0535], "cumulative_logprob": -18.1752, "norm_logp": -0.1874, "input_len": 390, "output_tokens": 97, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "106", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "time_sec": 2.956, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487,