{"id": "113", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of it. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. After these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner. If the original certificate is lost, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "time_sec": 2.847, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 1526, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 11064, 315, 15278, 624, 18, 13, 362, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 