{"id": "125", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "pred": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\n\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "time_sec": 9.463, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 518, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 6839, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 23, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 11, 979, 9334, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 24, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 24354, 15336, 525, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19, 7541, 6884, 11, 448, 279, 2999, 311, 9225, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.147, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0148, -0.0006, -0.1956, -0.5338, -0.0004, -0.0014, -0.0032