{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "time_sec": 1.989, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0754, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0167, -0.0037, -0.0725, -0.2017, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.6919, -0.254, -0.0005, -0.1094, -0.009, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.8565, -0.8839, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0088, -0.0021, -0.5587, -0.0005, -0.0507, -0.0013, -0.0009, -0.01, -0.0053, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.1509, -0.0144, -0.056, -0.0026, -0.0047, -0.0002, -0.2382, -0.6988, -0.4062, -0.2226, -1.6809, -0.054, -0.2647, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0091, -0.009, -0.0097, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.3124, -0.0305, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.2287, -0.9289], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1691, "norm_logp": -0.1389, "input_len": 648, "output_tokens": 66, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.12, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "time_sec": 2.125, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0754, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0167, -0.0037, -0.0725, -0.2017, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.6919, -0.254, -0.0005, -0.1094, -0.009, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.8565, -0.8839, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0088, -0.0021, -0.5587, -0.0005, -0.0507, -0.0013, -0.0009, -0.01, -0.0053, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.1509, -0.0144, -0.056, -0.0026, -0.0047, -0.0002, -0.2382, -0.6988, -0.4062, -0.2226, -1.6809, -0.054, -0.2647, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0091, -0.009, -0.0097, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.3124, -0.0305, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.2287, -0.9289], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1691, "norm_logp": -0.1389, "input_len": 648, "output_tokens": 66, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "146", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sew a zipper gusset:\n\n1. Make a casing in the side seams by stitching the outer edge of the gusset and the back side seam.\n2. Slide the boning right down into the casing.\n3. Push the seam allowance to the back and tack the casing to the lining, if necessary, so it doesn't move.\n4. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\n5. Sew across the top of the zipper sandwich with a zipper foot, making sure to line up the three edges.\n6. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper.\n7. Trace all pattern pieces to the remaining fabric and cut them out.\n8. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, with the right sides facing each other, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n9. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the zipper gusset, with the right sides facing down, and stitch along the seam line.\n10. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n11. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n12. The width of the zipper between the gusset should measure 1/2\".\n13. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch along the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics together nicely.\n\nTherefore, to sew a zipper gusset, you need to make a casing in the side seams, insert the boning, make a zipper sandwich, sew the zipper gusset to the zipper, and attach the lining to the zipper gusset.", "pred": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\n\n1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "time_sec": 8.167, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 678, 5383, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 21580, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 68761, 4478, 11, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 311, 279,