{"id": "206", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the given passages, Swiss chard (also known as just plain chard) is a type of beet plant that has been selected for its leaf production rather than storage root formation. It produces large, tender deep green leaves with thick, crisp stalks. The leaves have a more assertive and sometimes bitter taste compared to spinach. Swiss chard is a perishable vegetable and should be stored in the refrigerator. It can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.", "time_sec": 4.081, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 374, 264, 4462, 315, 279, 48012, 2997, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 29160, 39