{"id": "221", "question": "how to peel potatoes fast", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Boil the potatoes for about 15 minutes.\n3. Place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water and swish them around for a few seconds.\n4. Remove the potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAlternatively, you can also try the following method:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin, making a cut all around the potato lengthwise.\n2. Boil the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds.\n4. Rub the potato with both hands, and the skin should fall right off.\n\nThese methods should help you peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil for about 15 minutes.\n3. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the boiled potatoes in it.\n4. Swish the potatoes in the ice water for a few seconds to cool them down.\n5. Remove the potatoes from the ice water and peel the skin easily.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil for about 15 minutes.\n3. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the boiled potatoes in it.\n4. Swish the potatoes in the ice water for a few seconds to cool them down.\n5. Remove the potatoes from the ice water and peel the skin easily.", "time_sec": 3.721, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 57112, 34167, 4937, 1447, 16, 13, 18115, 279, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 448, 264, 21430, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 16548, 34167, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 18, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 279, 65085, 34167, 304, 432, 624, 19, 13, 4492, 812, 279, 34167, 304, 279, 9853, 3015, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 311, 7010, 1105, 1495, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 34167, 504, 279, 9853, 3015, 323, 57112, 279, 6787, 6707, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1213, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.016, -0.0004, -0.0765, -0.7648, -0.536, -0.5254, -0.0037, -0.0013, -0.0003, -0.0207, -0.3173, -0.081, -0.0038, -1.0671, -0.6041, -0.114, -0.5379, -0.2525, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.1367, -0.0009, -0.416, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0688, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.9562, -0.0178, -0.1672, -0.0003, -0.0143, -0.0527, -0.0802, -0.1021, -0.0219, -0.0, -0.6693, -0.128, -0.1272, -0.0323, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0905, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0183, -0.0082, -0.0013, -0.0006, -0.0088, -0.0005, -0.5273, -0.5004, -0.0171, -0.7259, -0.0003, -0.0236, -0.2816, -0.3573, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1022, -0.0005, -0.0526, -0.0063, -0.3965, -0.0037, -0.0368, -0.0004, -0.0864, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.5128, -0.108, -0.0242, -0.3434, -0.3685, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0227, -0.0316, -0.2556, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.2703, -0.0005, -0.2451, -1.9393, -0.7761, -0.0497, -1.5455, -1.0076, -0.0248], "cumulative_logprob": -18.8167, "norm_logp": -0.1863, "input_len": 539, "output_tokens": 101, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "224", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "time_sec": 10.371, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1171, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0188, -0.0004, -0.1794, -0.5907, -0.0013, -0.3925, -0.0018, -0.0472, -0.0032, -0.0448, -0.0017, -0.2621, -0.078, -0.0021, -0.0016, -0.2638, -0.0119, -0.0001, -0.3674, -0.0192, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0013, -0.0021, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.1095, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0093, -0.0002, -0.0012, -0.0073, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0349, -0.0044, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7608, -0.0026, -0.0, -0.1231, -0.3361, -0.5796, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0042, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0362, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.6253, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0089, -0.0017, -0.0046, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0409, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.1893, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0133, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.2462, -0.0222, -0.0, -0.0496, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0037, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0244, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.4453, -0.0648, -0.0707, -0.0, -0.006, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0437, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0414, -0.0003, -0.0035, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1052, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0185, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0234,