{"id": "231", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "pred": "Based on the given passages, there are several methods to remove oil stains from a concrete driveway. One method involves using a commercial-grade cleaner, scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then adding detergent to a pressure washer to spray the area evenly. Another method involves using a poultice method for fresh or stubborn stains. It is important to clean the area with water before applying any cleaner to remove dirt and debris. High pressure hoses should be avoided as they can push the oil deeper into the pavement.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, there are several methods to remove oil stains from a concrete driveway. One method involves using a commercial-grade cleaner, scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then adding detergent to a pressure washer to spray the area evenly. Another method involves using a poultice method for fresh or stubborn stains. It is important to clean the area with water before applying any cleaner to remove dirt and debris. High pressure hoses should be avoided as they can push the oil deeper into the pavement.", "time_sec": 3.436, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1052, 525, 3807, 5413, 311, 4057, 5590, 62463, 504, 264, 14175, 52142, 13, 3776, 1714, 17601, 1667, 264, 8353, 40227, 31881, 11, 44901, 7132, 448, 264, 15625, 476, 2896, 316, 11, 323, 1221, 7842, 90134, 311, 264, 7262, 52892, 311, 22899, 279, 3082, 41047, 13, 13293, 1714, 17601, 1667, 264, 16836, 4832, 558, 1714, 369, 7722, 476, 51396, 62463, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 4240, 279, 3082, 448, 3015, 1573, 18950, 894, 31881, 311, 4057, 25284, 323, 33998, 13, 5124, 7262, 95836, 1265, 387, 30790, 438, 807, 646, 4484, 279, 5590, 19117, 1119, 279, 64342, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0664, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0191, -0.0008, -0.1127, -1.2526, -0.002, -0.1547, -0.0392, -0.393, -0.1399, -0.0078, -0.0007, -0.0299, -0.1438, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.5105, -1.4969, -0.214, -0.2374, -0.4803, -0.404, -0.3107, -0.0067, -0.0012, -0.7749, -0.1622, -0.0003, -0.1823, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0069, -0.1942, -0.05, -0.1804, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.054, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.404, -0.1471, -0.424, -0.625, -0.6828, -0.5748, -0.5729, -0.0734, -0.95, -0.1496, -0.4441, -0.0216, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.4336, -0.4227, -0.0156, -0.0805, -0.1455, -0.5297, -0.1706, -1.0051, -0.3887, -0.8, -0.0801, -0.5461, -0.0296, -0.6727, -0.2366, -0.0123, -1.0379, -0.6088, -0.3389, -0.4843, -0.8649, -0.7345, -0.1358, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.4467, -1.0379, -0.2026, -0.0209, -0.0015, -0.4757, -0.0167, -0.503, -0.0021, -0.9382, -0.0136, -0.3151, -0.0127, -0.0213, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0344, -0.0049, -0.373], "cumulative_logprob": -26.8993, "norm_logp": -0.2612, "input_len": 569, "output_tokens": 103, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "235", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "pred": "- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 50 degrees in December.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, while Sausalito gets 0 inches of snow.\n- The average US city has 256 sunny days per year, while Sausalito has 256 sunny days per year.\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\n- Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, which is 30 points higher than the US average of 54.\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be described as follows:\n\n- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 50 degrees in December.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, while Sausalito gets 0 inches of snow.\n- The average US city has 256 sunny days per year, while Sausalito has 256 sunny days per year.\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\n- Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, which is 30 points higher than the US average of 54.\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.", "time_sec": 8.704, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 11017, 1447, 12, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 304, 6122, 624, 12, 576, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 304, 6652, 624, 12, 576, 1429, 15088, 59950, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 13666, 304, 6058, 448, 220, 15, 14924, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 5221, 220, 17, 21, 14924, 315, 11794, 817, 1042, 11, 1393, 328, 79074, 6357, 5221, 220, 15, 14924, 315, 11794, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 702, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 11, 1393, 328, 79074, 6357, 702, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 576, 5768, 1550, 374, 2163, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 6058, 3347, 374, 220, 19, 18, 12348, 624, 12, 328, 79074, 6357, 594, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 23, 19, 700, 315, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11, 892, 374, 220, 18, 15, 3501, 5080, 1091, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 2274, 5461, 369, 279, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 1922, 374, 3118, 389, 279, 2790, 1372, 315, 2849, 29071, 2878, 279, 6838, 2088, 315, 220, 22, 15, 12, 23, 15, 12348, 11, 323, 264, 16346, 374, 9251, 369, 2849, 315, 26541, 37093, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0272, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0178, -0.0003, -0.106, -0.576, -0.0215, -0.1857, -0.0211, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.6913, -0.0001, -0.7713, -0.0326, -0.0151, -0.1308, -0.7119, -0.9071, -0.2781, -0.117, -0.01, -0.0011, -0.2643, -0.5784, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.6341, -0.5955, -0.3142, -0.0091, -0.0011, -0.7613, -0.0026, -0.2703, -0.0002, -0.0013, -0.00