{"id": "245", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "time_sec": 2.192, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 1393, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0945, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0189, -0.0006, -0.0877, -0.3315, -1.0405, -0.0005, -0.4336, -0.0005, -0.3485, -0.0708, -0.4645, -0.1731, -0.4062, -0.0001, -0.6576, -0.015, -0.6062, -0.0117, -0.5518, -0.7788, -0.0124, -0.014, -0.0002, -0.0078, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0