{"id": "248", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "time_sec": 2.854, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 1393, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0945, -0