{"id": "259", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean dryer vent\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo clean the dryer vent, start by locating the vent cover on the outside of the house and removing it. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer and use a dryer vent brush to clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning the area around the lint filter for a more thorough cleaning. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits and ensure your dryer runs efficiently.\n\nIf the passages did not contain the necessary information to answer the question, I would have replied with \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "time_sec": 8.125, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 624, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 2