l": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "290", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Defrost the pork loin if possible. If you don't have time to defrost, you can place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour.\n2. Preheat the oven to 325°F (passage 2).\n3. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with 2 tsp of olive oil and season the outside with salt, pepper, and desired herbs (thyme, oregano, or garlic work well) (passage 2).\n4. Place the pork loin in a roasting pan and put it in the preheated oven (passage 2).\n5. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 150°F (passage 3).\n6. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature of the meat (passage 3).\n7. Once the meat is cooked, remove it from the oven and cover it with aluminum foil for 30 minutes before serving (passage 3).\n\nNote that the exact cooking time may vary depending on the size of the roast, so adjust the cooking time accordingly. Also, make sure to check the internal temperature of the meat to ensure that it is cooked all the way through.", "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "time_sec": 5.718, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 624, 18, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 624, 19, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 624, 20, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 24491, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.6229, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0445, -0.0022, -0.1755, -0.2004, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0026, -0.003, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.6568, -0.3557, -0.0021, -0.0073, -0.5529, -0.0029, -0.0001, -0.147, -0.0003, -0.429, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.0024, -0.0011, -0.0112, -0.0, -0.0038, -0.0032, -0.0582, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.6398, -0.0021, -0.0112, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.4632, -0.0002, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0493, -0.0077, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2739, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0952, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.0027, -0.0203, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0403, -0.0042, -0.0016, -0.0009, -0.0025, -0.0266, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0077, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.2777, -0.0005, -0.0,