{"id": "294", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "To properly fertilize your grass, you should fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for your specific grass type. For warm season grasses, this would be when the grass turns green in the early spring. You should also know the type of fertilizer to use based on the type of grass you have and do a pH soil test to ensure the fertilizer has the appropriate pH for your soil. Once you've determined the correct fertilizer and timing, apply it in a perpendicular pattern and check the lawn after application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape, but if it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "pred": "1. Timing: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\n2. Type of grass: Know your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer and frequency of application.\n3. Soil pH: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil, which helps in determining the appropriate pH for your fertilizer.\n4. Lawn size: Measure your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\n5. Application: Pour in the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern.\n6. Check: Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating that the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps:\n\n1. Timing: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\n2. Type of grass: Know your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer and frequency of application.\n3. Soil pH: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil, which helps in determining the appropriate pH for your fertilizer.\n4. Lawn size: Measure your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\n5. Application: Pour in the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern.\n6. Check: Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating that the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.", "time_sec": 7.67, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 70813, 25, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 369, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 624, 17, 13, 3990, 315, 16359, 25, 14187, 697, 16359, 943, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 64291, 323, 11639, 315, 3766, 624, 18, 13, 75519, 36043, 25, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 11, 892, 8609, 304, 25597, 279, 8311, 36043, 369, 697, 64291, 624, 19, 13, 68392, 1379, 25, 34104, 697, 36025, 311, 5978, 498, 614, 279, 1290, 3311, 315, 64291, 624, 20, 13, 7323, 25, 25968, 304, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 25, 14822, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 18860, 429, 279, 36025, 374, 304, 1661, 6083, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0628, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0117, -0.0006, -0.0419, -0.0482, -0.0016, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0341, -0.0009, -0.4779, -0.6202, -0.3843, -0.4108, -0.0031, -0.0001, -1.1863, -0.3102, -0.1538, -0.0, -0.013, -0.1638, -0.0001, -0.4964, -0.0008, -0.0101, -0.0893, -0.152, -0.6304, -0.2031, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0014, -0.0027, -0.0, -0.6688, -0.1006, -0.1015, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.5171, -0.2553