{"id": "340", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "pred": "3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\n1. **Grilled Ribs:**\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\n2. **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs:**\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\n\n3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "time_sec": 11.59, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 22471, 10823, 45277, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432,