{"id": "404", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "The passage provides step-by-step instructions for removing the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR. To perform this task, the passenger must locate and remove the two screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle. A pin on the outside edge of the door must also be removed using a door panel removal tool. Once all these steps are completed, the door panel can be carefully pulled away from the frame, taking care not to damage any wiring connections.\n\nAccordingly, the answer to the question is:\n\nRemoving the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR involves locating and removing the screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle, as well as removing the pin on the outside edge of the door using a door panel removal tool.", "pred": "1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\n8. The panel will come off the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\n8. The panel will come off the frame.", "time_sec": 5.005, "recor