": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "406", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "pred": "1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\n8. The panel will come off the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\n8. The panel will come off the frame.", "time_sec": 4.995, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 6945, 504, 264, 220,