{"id": "425", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, an UPDescription is:\n\n1. A barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. (Passage 1)\n2. A process involving receiving a specimen bottle from a member, ensuring it contains a minimum of 30 milliliters of urine, initialing the label in the member's presence, and verifying the information on the label and DD Form 2624 (a military form). (Passage 2)\n3. A barcode partner that provides GS1 Originated UPC and EAN codes, as well as a toll-free number and positive customer reviews. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "time_sec": 2.181, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 95129, 320, 58278, 5643, 6119, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 5257, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 11, 438, 817, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1771, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.015, -0.002, -0.0552, -0.2882, -0.5407, -0.1889, -0.0126, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0809, -0.0057, -0.0496, -0.0328, -0.0, -0.8112, -0.0055, -0.6341, -0.8746, -0.005, -0.2973, -0.0067, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0855, -0.0032, -0.01, -0.1186, -0.0179, -0.0, -0.0042, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0147, -0.0, -0.4518, -0.0092, -0.0099, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0008, -0.0112, -0.0, -0.0344, -0.3576, -0.1238, -0.4803, -0.873, -0.0063, -0.0072, -0.0506, -0.6801, -0.0, -0.0024, -0.0035, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.6517, -0.9802, -0.491, -0.0058, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0404, -0.4318], "cumulative_logprob": -10.0461, "norm_logp": -0.1456, "input_len": 538, "output_tokens": 69, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "428", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. They can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning they develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning they develop from two different eggs with each being fertilized by its own sperm cell. Monoamniotic twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization. Dizygotic twin pregnancies are more likely in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, aged between 30 and 40 years, of above average height and weight, and who have had several previous pregnancies.", "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\n\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins): This occurs when a single fertilized egg (zygote) splits into two embryos. This happens after the ninth day after fertilization. An example of this is conjoined twins, where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization, resulting in shared organs and a high mortality rate.\n\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "time_sec": 7.585, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 43636, 1648, 1096, 13666, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 320, 4246, 70, 1272, 8, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 390, 71154, 43636, 11, 1380, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 11220, 1147, 48765, 1272, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13666, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 12942, 304, 6094, 35753, 323, 264, 1550, 28428, 4379, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 43636, 1648, 1096, 8573, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 27061, 553, 9363, 1741, 438, 279, 5220, 594, 56878, 11, 4231, 11, 2608, 11, 4680, 11, 323, 3681, 81208, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 11, 892, 525, 10078, 803, 4363, 311, 12170, 304, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 7945, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 879, 525, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 11, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1706, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.011, -0.0006, -0.049, -0.0148, -0.5089, -0.1844, -0.4527, -0.3481, -0.5077, -0.0708, -0.636, -0.0031, -0.0015, -0.1423, -0.0137, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.7005, -0.8045, -0.0078, -0.0001, -0.2529, -0.7368, -0.5862, -0.0655, -0.0119, -0.5534, -0.3105, -0.3911, -0.001, -0.0043, -0.8191, -0.0028, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.1637, -0.2244, -0.0015, -0.0632, -1.0288, -0.7397, -1.6742, -1.1066, -0.0175, -0.0603, -0.0001, -0.4964, -0.000