{"id": "430", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how twins happen:\n\n* Monoamniotic twins: These twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization.\n* Conjoined twins: When the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs, it happens within 8 days of fertilization, and mortality is highest for conjoined twins due to the many complications resulting from shared organs.\n* Dizygotic twin pregnancies: These twins are slightly more likely to occur in women who are of West African descent (especially Yoruba), between the ages of 30 and 40, are taller and heavier than average, and have had several previous pregnancies.\n* Identical twins (monozygotic): These twins develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos.\n* Fraternal twins (dizygotic): These twins develop from two different eggs, and each twin is fertilized by its own sperm cell.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages: The passage does not provide information on the exact timing or mechanism of twinning beyond what is mentioned above.", "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\n\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins): This occurs when a single fertilized egg (zygote) splits into two embryos. This happens after the ninth day after fertilization. An example of this is conjoined twins, where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization, resulting in shared organs and a high mortality rate.\n\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "time_sec": 7.628, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 43636, 1648, 1096, 13666, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 320, 4246, 70, 1272, 8, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 390, 71154, 43636, 11, 1380, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 11220, 1147, 48765, 1272, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13666, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 12942, 304, 6094, 35753, 323, 264, 1550, 28428, 4379, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 43636, 1648, 1096, 8573, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 27061, 553, 9363, 1741, 438, 279, 5220, 594, 56878, 11, 4231, 11, 2608, 11, 4680, 11, 323, 3681, 81208, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 11, 892, 525, 10078, 803, 4363, 311, 12170, 304, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 7945, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 879, 525, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 11, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1706, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.011, -0.0006, -0.049, -0.0148, -0.5089, -0.1844, -0.4527, -0.3481, -0.5077, -0.0708, -0.636