{"id": "434", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean tarnished jewelry at home\":\n\nTo clean tarnished jewelry at home, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth in the solution. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse it in cool water and buff it with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water and apply it with a soft, lint-free cloth. You can also use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl and submerging the jewelry in it. Let it sit for a while, then remove and rinse it with cool water. Be sure to use a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds.", "pred": "4. For silver jewelry, you can pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. If your silver is lightly tarnished, the salt bath should take the tarnish right off. If you're cleaning a lot of jewelry at once, you can use more water. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use a few different methods:\n\n1. For items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n\n2. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (not paper towels, which can scratch).\n\n3. For diamonds, the best way to clean them is with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth.\n\n4. For silver jewelry, you can pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. If your silver is lightly tarnished, the salt bath should take the tarnish right off. If you're cleaning a lot of jewelry at once, you can use more water. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "time_sec": 10.035, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 2421, 2155, 5413, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 3589, 429, 525, 16234, 40530, 11, 89394, 11, 476, 5916, 311, 2560, 789, 11, 6514, 264, 2421, 21025, 315, 23034, 12000, 26785, 448, 8205, 3015, 323, 23604, 279, 30717, 304, 264, 8413, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 30717, 11, 1221, 73241, 304, 7010, 3015, 323, 11522, 448, 264, 27292, 3080, 9058, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 43822, 86480, 812, 11, 6514, 264, 24937, 315, 2326, 5479, 27815, 38862, 311, 825, 949, 3015, 13, 44856, 279, 14961, 323, 3796, 279, 31881, 448, 264, 8413, 11, 57920, 12577, 27292, 320, 1921, 5567, 52884, 11, 892, 646, 18778, 3593, 18, 13, 1752, 48051, 11, 279, 1850, 1616, 311, 4240, 1105, 374, 448, 8205, 773, 9667, 3015, 323, 264, 8413, 30117, 28300, 15625, 476, 2310, 25507, 36061, 13, 7135, 432, 9058, 448, 264, 8413, 27292, 382, 19, 13, 1752, 14961, 30717, 11, 498, 646, 4914, 1378, 25374, 315, 4017, 3015, 1119, 264, 19212, 13, 1096, 1714, 4278, 438, 264, 21700, 34194, 261, 429, 28160, 86480, 812, 2041, 668, 81, 2228, 279, 14961, 13, 1416, 697, 14961, 374, 33404, 86480, 3304, 11, 279, 12021, 8885, 1265, 1896, 279, 86480, 812, 1290, 1007, 13, 1416, 498, 2299, 15826, 264, 2696, 315, 30717, 518, 3055, 11, 498, 646, 990, 803, 3015, 13, 1752, 1101, 825, 6573, 315, 30717, 11, 990, 2686, 3015, 13, 1416, 697, 30717, 702, 18747, 32510, 11, 1281, 2704, 807, 2765, 944, 387