{"id": "460", "question": "how the colonists respond to the stamp act. why was it so upsetting?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the colonists responded to the Stamp Act of 1765 with a mix of violent and non-violent protests. They held peaceful protests, chanting slogans such as \"No Taxation without Representation,\" but these were often met with violence from British soldiers, known as Red Coats, who would come to cause fights and make arrests. The colonists also organized public protests, legislative resolutions, town meetings, and boycotts of British goods throughout the colonies. The Stamp Act was seen as particularly egregious because it was the first direct tax imposed by Parliament on the colonies, and it required the use of tax-stamped paper for all newspapers, legal documents, and other printed materials. The colonists felt that this was an overreach of British authority and a violation of their rights as British subjects. The Act was eventually repealed in 1766, but it had already sparked widespread outrage and resistance among the colonists, contributing to the growing tensions that would eventually lead to the American Revolution.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the colonists responded to the Stamp Act in various ways, both violent and non-violent. They initially protested peacefully by holding signs and chanting slogans like \"No Taxation without Representation.\" However, some of the Red Coats would come along to cause a fight and get people arrested. The Stamp Act was so upsetting because it was the first direct tax imposed on the colonists, requiring the use of tax-stamped paper for all newspapers, legal documents, etc. This was seen as a violation of their rights and a way for the British government to exert control over the colonies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the colonists responded to the Stamp Act in various ways, both violent and non-violent. They initially protested peacefully by holding signs and chanting slogans like \"No Taxation without Representation.\" However, some of the Red Coats would come along to cause a fight and get people arrested. The Stamp Act was so upsetting because it was the first direct tax imposed on the colonists, requiring the use of tax-stamped paper for all newspapers, legal documents, etc. This was seen as a violation of their rights and a way for the British government to exert control over the colonies.", "time_sec": 4.407, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 14889, 1671, 16441, 311, 279, 54787, 3218, 304, 5257, 5510, 11, 2176, 16401, 323, 2477, 75727, 306, 13, 2379, 15102, 69405, 66779, 553, 9963, 11929, 323, 76574, 77001, 1075, 330, 2753, 15190, 367, 2041, 78046, 1189, 4354, 11, 1045, 315, 279, 3731, 3539, 1862, 1035, 2525, 3156, 311, 5240, 264, 4367, 323, 633, 1251, 12517, 13, 576, 54787, 3218, 572, 773, 89969, 1576, 432, 572, 279, 1156, 2118, 3742, 25980, 389, 279, 14889, 1671, 11, 22703, 279, 990, 315, 3742, 5477, 32198, 5567, 369, 678, 31494, 11, 5777, 9293, 11, 4992, 13, 1096, 572, 3884, 438, 264, 19940, 315, 862, 3188, 323, 264, 1616, 369, 279, 7855, 3033, 311, 42744, 2524, 916, 279, 47928, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0519, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0085, -0.0013, -0.0472, -0.0243, -0.0042, -0.0, -0.4479, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0455, -0.0002, -0.7228, -0.6789, -0.005, -0.1357, -0.437, -0.1763, -0.0, -0.0062, -0.0079, -0.0, -0.0285, -1.4458, -1.1692, -0.7471, -0.0126, -0.5927, -0.0113, -0.0008, -0.036, -0.0531, -0.5878, -0.5742, -0.0154, -0.0005, -0.0488, -0.0, -0.0355, -0.0867, -0.0433, -0.6329, -0.0, -1.4757, -1.453, -0.2814, -0.7997, -0.0499, -0.0005, -0.507, -0.5204, -0.1161, -0.2759, -0.0827, -0.355, -0.0014, -0.3241, -0.1913, -0.0016, -0.0001, -1.0327, -0.6789, -0.172, -0.0, -0.1919, -1.435, -0.0078, -0.3266, -0.004, -0.0967, -0.0144, -0.001, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.5276, -0.0032, -0.0088, -0.0, 