{"id": "489", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "time_sec": 4.712, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 