{"id": "493", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can tell who liked your tweet:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm to track who has favorited your tweets. These websites show you a list of users who have favorited your tweets, allowing you to see who has shown interest in your content.\n\nPassage 2 provides a step-by-step guide on how to track who favorited your tweets. According to the passage, you can use a simple web-based website to check who favorited your tweets. Once you have access to this website, you can enter your tweet's URL to view a list of users who have favorited it.\n\nPassage 3 does not provide any information on tracking who favorited your tweets. However, it does mention that you can set up your Twitter account to notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\n\nIn summary, to tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or set up your Twitter account to notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "time_sec": 4.787, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 429, 13918, 4694, 1608, 23150, 13, 3776, 1741, 3910, 9733, 374, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 13, 2014, 990, 419, 3910, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 728, 311, 6271, 905, 11, 1487, 304, 448, 697, 6271, 5934, 323, 3552, 11, 4205, 389, 697, 6271, 829, 7407, 389, 279, 8416, 1290, 1424, 9131, 315, 697, 2692, 594, 5379, 2150, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 11296, 2999, 429, 7952, 304, 279, 5943, 14875, 5022, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 389, 279, 6303, 52938, 2656, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 4171, 13, 1096, 686, 2138, 498, 311, 738, 705, 697, 2692, 773, 429, 498, 2299, 29216, 4566, 2551, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 825, 315, 862, 26574, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0901, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0359, -0.0014, -0.065, -0.3914, -0.0018, -0.1752, -0.0003, -0.0013, -0.0025, -0.0095, -0.0659, -0.3186, -1.0194, -0.1961, -0.7874, -1.0179, -1.398, -0.019, -0.0011, -0.3099, -1.494, -0.2646, -0.1156, -0.6045, -0.5238, -0.0581, -0.0066, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.4447, -0.9215, -0.2385, -0.3623, -0.3106, -0.0311, -0.3779, -0.3177, -0.0013, -1.0555, -0.0014, -0.2885, -0.0435, -0.5765, -0.0037, -0.0006, -0.0543, -0.0, -0.1182, -0.0051, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0431, -0.3989, -0.0001, -0.0214, -0.0063, -0.0012, -0.6826, -0.085, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0033, -0.5848, -0.0008, -0.0061, -0.0142, -0.0013, -0.014, -0.0275, -0.0