{"id": "534", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for the following purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to create a makeshift arm sling (Passage 2).\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg (Passage 2).\n3. Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances (Passage 2).\n4. Removing splinters (Passage 3).\n\nThe passages mention these specific uses for safety pins in a first aid context, but do not provide any additional information regarding their use in a survival kit.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for several purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\n3. Keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\n4. Removing splinters in the wilderness.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for several purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\n3. Keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\n4. Removing splinters in the wilderness.", "time_sec": 2.796, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 7149, 26944, 304, 264, 1156, 12296, 3745, 525, 1483, 369, 3807, 9895, 1447, 16, 13, 15335, 27929, 4849, 458, 6773, 553, 8983, 1229, 279, 74423, 315, 264, 1293, 36153, 15478, 311, 1181, 15138, 311, 11153, 264, 86080, 6773, 87633, 624, 17, 13, 4520, 1677, 264, 7055, 3362, 916, 264, 27493, 323, 34663, 6773, 476