{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "time_sec": 3.892, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 31