{"id": "611", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to create an employee schedule:\n\n1. Talk to a lawyer about work laws: It is important to understand the legal requirements for creating an employee schedule, including paying overtime for hours worked beyond 40 per week. Additionally, there may be other laws to consider, such as restrictions for employees under the age of 18.\n2. Use scheduling software or a simple word processing program: You can create an employee schedule using scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or even a sheet of paper. Make a list of all employees and their duties, and create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\n3. Print or send schedules to employees: Once you have created the schedule, print out copies for each employee or send them to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule for making any changes. If you are using a digital tool, you can easily edit and share the schedule with employees.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to create an employee schedule, such as setting up the schedule format, determining pay rates, or communicating the schedule to employees.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "time_sec": 3.948, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 5100, 21029, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 3060, 1667, 279, 9700, 3811, 438, 697, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1958, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0247, -0.0015, -0.1064, -0.6029, -0.2403, -0.2584, -0.0002, -0.2479, -0.2399, -0.0027, -0.0012, -0.5511, -0.0091, -0.0031, -0.1134, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.2067, -0.0001, -0.005, -0.0269, -0.0013, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.1952, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.1898, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0417, -0.0206, -0.0002, -0.0111, -0.0015, -0.0138, -0.0026, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.3969, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.4505, -0.0008, -0.0014, -0.1032, -0.0128, -0.0103, -0.001, -0.017, -0.0009, -0.0807, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0416, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.042, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.2075, -0.2542, -0.0163, -0.0231, -0.5364, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.1784, -1.0755, -0.0, -0.0591, -0.0041, -0.0057, -0.0028, -0.0, -0.0136, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.5893, -0.6993, -0.3099, -0.0001, -0.1936, -0.3136, -0.0006, -0.0317, -0.0003, -0.0051, -0.0196, -0.0002, -0.0068, -0.0859, -0.0042], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1278, "norm_logp": -0.0904, "input_len": 396, "output_tokens": 101, "eval_metrics": {"Token-