{"id": "615", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Passage 2 provides the necessary information to force removal of a printer in devices and printers. You can do this by first clicking on Control Panel, then selecting Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking on Printers. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you are unable to delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "time_sec": 3.226, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 10428, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 498, 4157, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 624, 22, 13, 9189, 6452, 438, 28093, 624, 23, 13, 9189, 10428, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2435, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0393, -0.0011, -0.1191, -0.2225, -0.0861, -0.2453, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -