{"id": "630", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to guard a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall, skilled shooter when guarding them near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player.\n\nTherefore, to guard a tall person in basketball, it is essential to stay close to them, move quickly laterally to maintain position, and use a defensive strategy such as keeping a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player, especially near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\n4. Use tips from an experienced basketball player to improve your defense.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player, especially near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\n4. Use tips from an experienced basketball player to improve your defense.", "time_sec": 3.09, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 1447, 16, 13, 28737, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 2781, 11, 5310, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 624, 17, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 624, 18, 13, 13655, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 10414, 504, 458, 10321, 19240, 2781, 311, 7269, 697, 9055, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1952, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0137, -0.0009, -0.1076, -0.1296, -0.0118, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0145, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.4786, -0.556, -0.0475, -1.0801, -0.0109, -0.0002, -0.0283, -0.2307, -0.0006, -0.0088, -0.0002, -0.0066, -0.5678, -0.019, -0.4441, -1.2644, -0.6205, -0.21, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.1488, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0657, -0.0002, -0.058, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0181, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.007, -0.2882, -0.0252, -0.1856, -0.0004, -0.4086, -0.0339, -0.4407, -0.0001, -0.0536, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.7057, -0.0042, -0.0156, -0.0019, -0.0008, -0.0025, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0165, -0.0127, -1.1262, -0.0046, -0.0, -1.3478, -0.6078, -0.1417, -0.1333, -0.0, -0.0049, -0.0005, -0.6775, -0.7035, -0.0187, -0.2958, -0.7953, -0.0108], "cumulative_logprob": -14.4158, "norm_logp": -0.1696, "input_len": 395, "output_tokens": 85, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "632", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "pred": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\n\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\n\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\n\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "time_sec": 7.27, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 785, 11799, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1604, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0092, -0.0003, -0.228, -0.1906, -0.9115, -0.2022, -0.0006, -0.0051, -0.0182, -0.0001, -0.0434, -0.0032, -0.0, -0.0, -0.6428, -1.0341, -0.2519, -0.0007, -0.0358, -0.1363, -0.1655, -0.389, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4572, -0.0026, -0.0028, -0.0008, -0.0155, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0028, -0.0023, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0334, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0245, -0.0238, -0.0213, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1846, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0135, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.1043, -0.0085, -0.0019, -0.002