{"id": "634", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the nervous system and endocrine system have some similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n- Both systems are responsible for maintaining homeostasis in the body.\n- Both systems use chemical messengers to coordinate and regulate the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Negative feedback mechanisms are used to regulate both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses while transmission in the endocrine system is done through chemicals called hormones.\n- The nervous system is a continuous network of interconnected cells while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs that are not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "pred": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\n\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\n\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\n\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "time_sec": 6.785, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 785, 11799, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1604, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0092, -0.0003, -0.228, -0.1906, -0.9115, -0.2022, -0.0006, -0.0051, -0.0182, -0.0001, -0.0434, -0.003