 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "645", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "pred": "1. Prepare the planting area by turning the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and breaking it up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris.\n2. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\n3. Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\n4. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Ensure the sprouted or eye side of the cubes is facing up.\n5. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\n\n1. Prepare the planting area by turning the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and breaking it up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris.\n2. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\n3. Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\n4. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Ensure the sprouted or eye side of the cubes is facing up.\n5. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.", "time_sec": 5.959, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 47014, 3082, 553, 13054, 279, 17171, 916, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 14719, 432, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 624, 17, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 624, 18, 13, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 13, 29279, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 315, 279, 54104, 374, 12880, 705, 624, 20, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1397, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0399, -0.002, -0.1586, -0.2185, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.2556, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.309, -0.232, -0.0035, -0.0352, -0.5536, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.9681, -0.0567, -0.4231, -0.0103, -0.3724, -0.0358, -0.1488, -0.0, -0.1205, -0.2148, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0101, -0.0005, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0028, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.4323, -0.1483, -0.733, -0.0026, -0.0053, -0.1779, -0.0204, -0.1014, -0.0038, -0.0001, -0.0208, -0.6937, -0.0, -0.7343, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.2228, -0.0028, -0.0011, -0.0974, -0.0001, -0.0042, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0075, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4835, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.4251, -0.1528, -0.263, -0.0008, -0.0945,