{"id": "659", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Vinegar can be used to improve a dog's skin and coat, clean out their ears, repel fleas, and soothe itchy ears.", "pred": "4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\n\n1. To improve the skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture can also be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\n\n2. To clean ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\n\n3. To repel fleas: Spray the dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas. Additionally, a flea comb can be used to remove fleas after spraying the coat.\n\n4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "time_sec": 6.508, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 25, 19219, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 323, 990, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 1096, 20980, 646, 1083, 387, 77621, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 4240, 24230, 25, 52767, 10607, 23268, 65055, 46105, 448, 220, 20, 15, 3266, 3015, 5707, 264, 6291, 369, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 5443, 264, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 279, 79603, 46105, 3