{"id": "663", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Sure, here are some possible answers based on the given passages:\n\nQ: What are some uses for vinegar when it comes to dogs?\n\nA: Vinegar can be used to:\n\n* Improve a dog's skin and coat by mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and using it as a final rinse.\n* Normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin by spraying full-strength vinegar on its coat.\n* Repel fleas by spraying a dog's coat with apple cider vinegar.\n* Soothe itchy ears by using a diluted solution of apple cider vinegar (50% water, 50% vinegar) on a cotton swab or gauze pad.\n* Clean a dog's ears by using apple cider vinegar.\n* Fight fleas by bathing a dog in a soap mixture that includes apple cider vinegar.\n* Remove fleas using a flea comb after bathing a dog in an apple cider vinegar soap mixture.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\n\n1. To improve the skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture can also be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\n\n2. To clean ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\n\n3. To repel fleas: Spray the dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas. Additionally, a flea comb can be used to remove fleas after spraying the coat.\n\n4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "time_sec": 7.198, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 25, 19219, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 323, 990, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 1096, 20980, 646, 1083, 387, 77621, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 4240, 24230, 25, 52767, 10607, 23268, 65055, 46105, 448, 220, 20, 15, 3266, 3015, 5707, 264, 6291, 369, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 5443, 264, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 279, 79603, 46105, 311, 43176, 1782, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 1416, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 22334, 11, 432, 1231, 13216, 458, 56496, 12720, 311, 2494, 304, 279, 5562, 594, 9968, 382, 18, 13, 2014, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 25, 60561, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 448, 46105, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 13, 22406, 11, 264, 95855, 3614, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 4057, 12962, 300, 1283, 82536, 279, 22875, 382, 19, 13, 2014, 4367, 12962, 300, 25, 16098, 383, 279, 5562, 304, 264, 20980, 315, 10584, 53, 33019, 391, 311, 4367, 12962, 300, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.033, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0188, -0.0004, -0.07, -0.1359, -0.6659, -0.0041, -0.0009, -0.1073, -0.2244, -0.0716, -0.4801, -0.0044, -0.3446, -0.0081, -0.0008, -0.8308, -0.1319, -0.5708, -0.4939, -0.0123, -0.0008, -0.8821, -1.2615, -0.0292, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0065, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2415, -0.0063, -0.336, -0.0002, -0.0064, -0.0, -1.1277, -0.7413, -0.0, -0.0112, -0.1011, -0.012, -0.1531, -0.0028, -0.7148, -0.1612, -0.3869, -0.0016, -0.0054, -0.003, -0.8821, -1.141, -1.4538, -0.4084, -0.5857, -0.2193, -0.3899, -0.2469, -0.0718, -0.0, -0.0409, -0.0052, -0.0208, -0.07, -0.0001, -0.0341, -0.0122, -0.2741, -0.0344, -0.0021, -0.0571, -0.0066, -0.0, -0.2485, -0.0014, -0