{"id": "675", "question": "inventory costing weighted average", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to your question:\n\nThe weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. The cost of goods available for sale is divided by the number of units available for sale to calculate the weighted-average cost per unit. This figure is then used to assign a cost to both ending inventory and the cost of goods sold. The weighted average method is commonly used when inventory items are intermingled and cannot be assigned a specific cost, or when the accounting system is not sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. This method takes the average cost of all inventories currently available and assigns it to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change. This method is commonly used in situations where inventory items are so intermingled that it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sufficiently sophisticated to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. This method takes the average cost of all inventories currently available and assigns it to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change. This method is commonly used in situations where inventory items are so intermingled that it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sufficiently sophisticated to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "time_sec": 3.822, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 36824, 5461, 1714, 315, 15444, 53724, 49912, 458, 5461, 2783, 311, 1817, 6573, 315, 15444, 979, 432, 374, 6088, 13, 1096, 1714, 4990, 279, 5461, 2783, 315, 678, 17023, 2433, 5023, 2500, 323, 49912, 432, 311, 279, 1509, 6088, 13, 8704, 15444, 7576, 38288, 6292, 11, 279, 36824, 5461, 2783, 686, 1083, 2297, 13, 1096, 1714, 374, 16626, 1483, 304, 14740, 1380, 15444, 3589, 525, 773, 946, 5311, 832, 429, 432, 374, 11997, 311, 9793, 264, 3151, 2783, 311, 458, 3842, 4982, 11, 476, 979, 279, 23168, 1849, 374, 537, 38944, 26779, 311, 3754, 47007, 476, 444, 25997, 15444, 13617, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1369, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0158, -0.0017, -0.0873, -0.446, -0.2331, -0.0013, -0.0399, -0.0606, -0.0814, -0.0007, -0.1716, -0.0555, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0065, -0.0016, -0.0502, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0072, -0.0046, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0343, -0.5074, -0.5285, -0.7621, -0.2016, -0.0022, -0.0455, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.1837, -0.0, -0.0014, -0.0, -1.0889, -0.0578, -0.4483, -0.0161, -0.0104, -0.0231, -0.0083, -0.0597, -0.9729, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0158, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0031, -0.0009, -0.0008, -0.0017, -0.1437, -0.0306, -0.0003, -0.0793, -0.8164, -0.0901, -0.021, -0.0863, -0.0002, -0.2323, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0.1171, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.1622, -0.0006, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.001, -0.0029, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3228, -0.354, -0.4229, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0141, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.013, -0.0299, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0139, -0.4863], "cumulative_logprob": -9.8338, "norm_logp": -0.0902, "input_len": 630, "output_tokens": 109, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "679", "question": "benefits and side effects of drinking clove tea", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here are the benefits and side effects of drinking clove tea:\n\nBenefits:\n\n* Soothes the senses and relieves stress (Passage 1)\n* Provides relief from pain due to muscle, joint, or ligament injuries (Passage 2)\n* Soothes abdominal pain and aids in digestion (Passage 3)\n\nSide Effects:\n\n* None mentioned in the passages.\n\nNote that there are no side effects mentioned in the passages provided. However, it's important to note that consuming clove tea in large quantities can cause irritation to the stomach and digestive tract, so it's best to consume it in moderation.", "pred": "There are no side effects mentioned in the provided passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of drinking clove tea include:\n\n1. Soothing the senses and relieving stress in the body.\n2. Providing relief from stress when mixed with basil, mint, and cardamom in water and taken with honey.\n3. Having skin benefits, although specific details are not provided.\n4. Relieving pain from muscle, joint, or ligament injuries due to its analgesic effects.\n5. Being applied to unbroken skin for pain relief.\n6. Working better with arthritic pain when applied as a warm tea compress.\n7. Soothing abdominal pain and aiding in digestion for those suffering from gas pain or other stomach upset.\n8. Stimulating blood flow, saliva production, and gastric secretions to aid in digestion.\n\nThere are no side effects mentioned in the provided passages.", "time_sec": 6.09, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 7567, 315, 16163, 5292, 586, 15243, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 2055, 78, 1596, 279, 37107, 323, 58544, 4405, 8464, 304, 279, 2487, 624, 17, 13, 80100, 15957, 504, 8464, 979, 9519, 448, 67086, 11, 28337, 11, 323, 3701, 309, 316, 