{"id": "692", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "gt": "No, based on the given passages, it does not seem like watching Snapchat stories directly increases one's score. However, sending and receiving more snaps, including opening all received snaps, can help increase the score.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "time_sec": 1.699, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 55179, 5456, 13, 576, 46769, 6286, 429, 279, 5456, 374, 264, 2629, 315, 279, 1372, 315, 51304, 3208, 323, 51304, 3949, 11, 323, 1052, 374, 902, 27039, 429, 10099, 7343, 42972, 311, 419, 5456, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2988, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0478, -0.0014, -0.0191, -0.1069, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.022, -0.0069, -0.2654, -0.5487, -0.5789, -0.0005, -0.0227, -0.2342, -0.8719, -1.4827, -0.1677, -0.6467, -0.2407, -0.0228, -0.8715, -0.0116, -0.0002, -0.0129, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0031, -0.0134, -0.0003, -0.209, -0.0, -0.3981, -0.3194, -0.9232, -0.0387, -0.0032, -0.4292, -0.0171, -0.5258, -0.0213, -0.4007, -0.0005, -1.1539, -0.8797, -0.0137, -0.1439], "cumulative_logprob": -11.9797, "norm_logp": -0.2445, "input_len": 564, "output_tokens": 49, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "695", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, you start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Next, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\n\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\n\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "time_sec": 7.769, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 279, 11116, 421, 498, 1366, 803, 382, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19187, 848, 11, 23065, 3786, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 19, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 13, 910, 399, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1423, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0192, -0.0007, -0.1253, -0.8282, -0.5741, -0.1317, -0.5772, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.1355, -0.0217, -0.0026, -1.68, -0.227, -1.1069, -0.3794, -0.6575, -0.0004, -0.3007, -0.3985, -1.9093, -0.5729, -0.0531, -0.7733, -0.4329, -0.6147, -0.0, -0.0278, -0.2838, -0.2766, -0.6861, -0.0021, -0.3951, -0.0006, -1.2885, -0.0657, -0.0333, -0.9146, -0.0009, -0.0039, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0001, -0.0244, -0.1439, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0024, -0.001, -0.9609, -1.2432, -0.3579, -1.2167, -0.6695, -0.0069, -0.0, -0.0267, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.1687, -0.2034, -0.7871, -0.253, -0.0094, -0.6479, -0.0873, -0.1017, -0.0437, -0.4074