{"id": "702", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers and pouring water. Water play also provides opportunities for academic learning, such as understanding concepts like floating and sinking, measuring water, and comparing quantities. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children pretend and engage in imaginative play with water.", "pred": "1. Gross motor skills: Children run through sprinklers, fill and pour water, and engage in physical activities that enhance their gross motor skills.\n2. Academic learning: Water play helps with science by teaching concepts like floating and sinking, and with math by practicing measuring and comparing quantities of water.\n3. Creativity: Children use their imagination and pretend while playing with water, fostering creative thinking and expression.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, children learn several things with water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Children run through sprinklers, fill and pour water, and engage in physical activities that enhance their gross motor skills.\n2. Academic learning: Water play helps with science by teaching concepts like floating and sinking, and with math by practicing measuring and comparing quantities of water.\n3. Creativity: Children use their imagination and pretend while playing with water, fostering creative thinking and expression.", "time_sec": 2.801, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2841, 3960, 3807, 2513, 448, 3015, 1486, 1447, 16, 13, 42807, 8872, 7361, 25, 15044, 1598, 1526, 50698, 9254, 11, 5155, 323, 4914, 3015, 11, 323, 16579, 304, 6961, 7488, 429, 18379, 862, 19952, 8872, 7361, 624, 17, 13, 41070, 6832, 25, 9959, 1486, 8609, 448, 8038, 553, 12629, 18940, 10